{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits","id":786694,"title":"Homebrew Demon Merits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-15T06:55:21-08:00","id":786694,"title":"Homebrew Demon Merits","content":"My thread for any Homebrew Demon Merits I put together, as well as for others to critique them. If you guys happen to have any interesting homebrew material you'd like to share, feel free to drop them here. And now, I start off with my first submission, which I thought up in response to Unchained needing to revert back to human form before they can do new combinations for partial transformation. <hr /><br /> <b>Flexible Transformation (o)<br /> Effect:</b> Your ability to perform partial transformations has been refined to the point that you can swap out active form abilities for new ones as the situation demands. This requires both the expenditure of 1 Aether and a reflexive Resolve + Composure roll, with a -2 penalty for each form ability to be swapped out.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback:</b> This type of transformation calls for a compromise roll, regardless of whether or not it succeeds","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 12-22-2015, 07:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T07:47:57-08:00","id":786720,"title":"","content":"Primum + Willpower? Really?<br /> <br /> Needs an example, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T10:54:37-08:00","id":786795,"title":"","content":"I have been thinking of removing the dice roll, or even just changing it to Willpower only.<br /> <br /> And by an example, do you mean a brief description for how this Merit should work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T11:38:04-08:00","id":786816,"title":"","content":"It's not 'Willpower'. At most it'd be Resolve + Composure. Nobody rolls Willpower in CofD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T11:51:46-08:00","id":786828,"title":"","content":"I think he means that Willpower really isn't used itself in dice pools (Resolve + Composure, which Willpower is derived from, is used instead). While Willpower has a dot rating, it is also a derived attribute <i>and</i> a fuel stat (kind of).<br /> <br /> (This hasn't stopped me from considering the use of Willpower as a dice pool mechanic, solely for the considerations brought on by those who &quot;spend&quot; their Willpower dots on things)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T12:27:59-08:00","id":786849,"title":"","content":"Merits, eh?<ul><li>This isn't a new one, but rather a modification: Have Status [Agency] grant benefits similar to Mystery Cults, thus serving as a mechanical Z-splat for Demons (as it currently serves as solely as a narrative one).</li> <li><b>Overcharge Embed</b> \u2022\u2022: Allows the Demon to spend 1 Aether to add their Primum to an Embed rolls.<ul><li><u>Creator's Notes</u>: Used for when a Demon needs more dice, but doesn't want a full Exploit. Still triggers the senses of anything that detects Aether.<ul><li>Addendum: I'm not sure if Overclocking does this already. Can't remember.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li><b>Soul Collector</b> \u2022\u2022\u2022: Most Demons interact with &quot;souls&quot; merely as a means to the end of taking a mortal identity as a Cover. Some have figured out how to capture the Soul most mortals (and other beings) would recognize as such, and store it in a contract. Such Demons do a brisk trade with other Unchained in need of a Soul-soul (such as replacing the one their Stigmatic agent burnt out using a Form gadget, or a &quot;filler&quot; for Raise Dead), and other supernaturals that have an interest in such commodities (such as Mage Reapers).<ul><li><u>Creator's Notes</u>: This is used for allowing Unchained to interact with souls proper (as in, the lack of which causing the Soul-less Condition), and as a spring-board for additional soul manipulation (harvesting for Aether, using as insulation for Compromise checks, transforming into a ephemeral Cryptid, etc.)</li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Implant Tolerance</b> \u2022\u2022\u2022: The Stigmatic can endure the addition of, and use, an Implanted Gadget just like a Demon. While they do not suffer Compromise rolls for being seen with it, they do provoke Integrity checks in others, as well as uncomfortable questions and the Surveilled Condition.</span></span></span><ul><li><u>Creator's Notes</u>: <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">For giving your favored Stigmatic agent that mind control eye or gun hand they've always wanted.</span></span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Gadgeteer</b> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022: Character can install Embeds (and even Exploits, if any) they have access to into objects just like a Demon (Bits of their soul are used instead of Primum).</span></span></span><ul><li><u>Creator's Notes</u>: <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Useful for Stigmatic and Demon-blooded only groups (such as potential Hunter organizations) to have a few tricks up their sleeves. Requires Sleeve Integrators or Offspring/Fractals so as to have access to Embeds with which to Install. May require access to Aether for processes that require it.</span></span></span></li> </ul></li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 12-15-2015, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T20:10:16-08:00","id":787109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=786816#post786816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not 'Willpower'. At most it'd be Resolve + Composure. Nobody rolls Willpower in CofD.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=786828#post786828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think he means that Willpower really isn't used itself in dice pools (Resolve + Composure, which Willpower is derived from, is used instead). While Willpower has a dot rating, it is also a derived attribute <i>and</i> a fuel stat (kind of).<br /> <br /> (This hasn't stopped me from considering the use of Willpower as a dice pool mechanic, solely for the considerations brought on by those who &quot;spend&quot; their Willpower dots on things)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I meant Resolve + Composure as the dice pool.<br /> <br /> That said, regarding Flexible Transformation. Say, you have three form abilities active via partial transformation. Rather than having to revert to human form if you need to switch out those forms for others, you instead roll the dice pool (and any penalties if it's not just one ability to be 'swapped'). On a success, the switch happens. On a failure, it doesn't.<br /> <br /> Trying to think up, though, what could happen for Dramatic Failures and Exceptional Success. So far, I was thinking that a Dramatic Failure might force you out into your full demonic form, maybe with the Aetheric Bleed Condition imposed and/or an inability to revert to human form for a certain duration?<br /> <br /> I've also been thinking of expanding the Flexible Transformation, too, or creating a separate Merit that allows for activating additional form abilities while in a partially transformed state? Any thoughts on this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T13:39:19-08:00","id":791059,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Advanced Self-Repair System 3 Dots</u></b><br /> <b>Perquisite: </b>Terrible Form (Style) 2 Dots<br /> The demons ability to heal between transformations is supported by a more advanced internal system. While transitioning into Full Transformation, the demon can spend aether to downgrade aggravated damage to lethal at a one-to-one cost. In Partial Transformation, the demon heals one extra box of health.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T17:12:41-08:00","id":791162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=786849#post786849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Overcharge Embed</b> \u2022\u2022: Allows the Demon to spend 1 Aether to add their Primum to an Embed rolls.<br /> <br /> <u>Creator's Notes</u>: Used for when a Demon needs more dice, but doesn't want a full Exploit. Still triggers the senses of anything that detects Aether.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it does, so this Merit actually can be a welcome addition. Especially for those games where Resistance may <i>always</i> apply against a given Embed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=786849#post786849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Implant Tolerance</b> \u2022\u2022\u2022: The Stigmatic can endure the addition of, and use, an Implanted Gadget just like a Demon. While they do not suffer Compromise rolls for being seen with it, they do provoke Integrity checks in others, as well as uncomfortable questions and the Surveilled Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume the Surveilled Condition would be persistent until the Gadget is removed from the Stigmatic?<br /> <br /> And on a semi-related note, has anyone ever checked if there's a limit to the number of Gadgets (especially Form Gadgets) that a Demon can install on himself?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 12-22-2015, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T19:29:41-08:00","id":791228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=786849#post786849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soul Collector \u2022\u2022\u2022: Most Demons interact with &quot;souls&quot; merely as a means to the end of taking a mortal identity as a Cover. Some have figured out how to capture the Soul most mortals (and other beings) would recognize as such, and store it in a contract. Such Demons do a brisk trade with other Unchained in need of a Soul-soul (such as replacing the one their Stigmatic agent burnt out using a Form gadget, or a &quot;filler&quot; for Raise Dead), and other supernaturals that have an interest in such commodities (such as Mage Reapers).<ul><li><u>Creator's Notes</u>: This is used for allowing Unchained to interact with souls proper (as in, the lack of which causing the Soul-less Condition), and as a spring-board for additional soul manipulation (harvesting for Aether, using as insulation for Compromise checks, transforming into a ephemeral Cryptid, etc.)</li> </ul><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Gadgeteer</b> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022: Character can install Embeds (and even Exploits, if any) they have access to into objects just like a Demon (Bits of their soul are used instead of Primum).</span></span></span><ul><li><u>Creator's Notes</u>: <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Useful for Stigmatic and Demon-blooded only groups (such as potential Hunter organizations) to have a few tricks up their sleeves. Requires Sleeve Integrators or Offspring/Fractals so as to have access to Embeds with which to Install. May require access to Aether for processes that require it.</span></span></span></li> </ul></li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Need more information on how these would work; even freely given, Demons are not designed to interact with souls and there should be a small chance by failure. Likewise most stigmatics do not have Embeds and neither groups can have Exploits so how do they install such things into items without knowing them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T19:38:43-08:00","id":791235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=791162#post791162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it does, so this Merit actually can be a welcome addition. Especially for those games where Resistance may <i>always</i> apply against a given Embed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. It's a minor change and the benefit comes with its own inherent drawbacks (consuming fuel and potential detection).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=791162#post791162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume the Surveilled Condition would be persistent until the Gadget is removed from the Stigmatic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I intended it to be until the Condition was resolved (one way or another), but re-applied if someone caught sight of their demonic cyber-implant again. Nice excuse to wear an eye-patch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=791162#post791162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And on a semi-related note, has anyone ever checked if there's a limit to the number of Gadgets (especially Form Gadgets) that a Demon can install on himself?</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I understand, no, not explicitly. Remember though, that Form Gadgets are <i>rare</i>. Most Demons don't even know the detail about creating them, and fewer would <i>want</i> to. <br /> <br /> Of course, if you wanted to create a fearsome &quot;headhunter&quot; Demon that grafts on the parts from their kills, or one that is the intra-Unchained version of a loan shark, feel free to use the character concept (I've got an Agency idea based around just that).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T19:49:53-08:00","id":791240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=791228#post791228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Need more information on how these would work; even freely given, Demons are not designed to interact with souls and there should be a small chance by failure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking it is pretty much a Soul Pact, just instead of the option to take them as a Cover at a later date, they instead capture the Soul in the Pact document itself (inflicting the Soulless Condition, thereby). Mostly intended as additional ideas for interacting with mortals, other supernaturals, and for odd plot uses. I identified the need/niche by some Demonic features referencing Souls (mortals burned by Form Gadgets, the Raise Dead Exploit), but Unchained having no real way of interacting with them. This would - at its most basic - allow that, in addition to &quot;traditional&quot; plots (such as &quot;a demon stole my soul - I need it back&quot;) and soul trading (for the hungry Lich or oddly palated spirit). The other proposed options were just for adding more use/value.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=791228#post791228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likewise most stigmatics do not have Embeds and neither groups can have Exploits so how do they install such things into items without knowing them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Stigmatics can gain Embeds via Sleeve Integrator, and Offspring/Fractals can acquire them &quot;normally&quot;. This just opens up Gadget creation to allow non-Demons to contribute. As for Exploits, as it stands currently, yes, they don't (barring the Forbidden Knowledge hack from Mirrors) - but additional material or homebrew might allow it, so I thought I'd spell it out as allowed here (though obviously limited by their normal inaccessability).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 12-22-2015, 10:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T02:33:55-08:00","id":793031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=791059#post791059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Advanced Self-Repair System 3 Dots</u></b><br /> <b>Perquisite: </b>Terrible Form (Style) 2 Dots<br /> The demons ability to heal between transformations is supported by a more advanced internal system. While transitioning into Full Transformation, the demon can spend aether to downgrade aggravated damage to lethal at a one-to-one cost. In Partial Transformation, the demon heals one extra box of health.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about heal bashing/lethal damage equal to half the character's Primum (rounded down)? I can also see a 5-dot version of this allowing you to treat aggravated damage as two lethal for the purpose of the healing brought about by the full transformation, while it allows you to heal Primum points of bashing/lethal damage when you take a partial transformation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T07:41:34-08:00","id":793081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=793031#post793031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How about heal bashing/lethal damage equal to half the character's Primum (rounded down)? I can also see a 5-dot version of this allowing you to treat aggravated damage as two lethal for the purpose of the healing brought about by the full transformation, while it allows you to heal Primum points of bashing/lethal damage when you take a partial transformation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think those are all reasonable suggestions. This whole thread has got me thinking aboout merits that modify the intrinsic capabilities of demons especially their demonic forms. Maybe there could be one that could allow the demon to use more aether per turn in demonic form? Stuff like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T07:53:25-08:00","id":793089,"title":"","content":"I was trying to figure out a system of allowing Demons to boost their Attributes. I figured letting them &quot;use&quot; their form abilities on a one-for-one basis (which would prevent usage of those abilities, and cap the total bonus).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T08:30:22-08:00","id":793105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=793089#post793089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was trying to figure out a system of allowing Demons to boost their Attributes. I figured letting them &quot;use&quot; their form abilities on a one-for-one basis (which would prevent usage of those abilities, and cap the total bonus).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have been struggling to figure something like this out since Demon: the Fallen came out. I think what the current game does well is that it does provide a lot of embeds that you can use to consistently improve rolls without paying any aether (Plus, you have legend to fool around with when you want to boost stats). If there were something to boost attributes I would see it more along the lines of a processes rather than a merit...now that I write that it could be interesting to have a merit that allows you to boost attributes through legend if that makes any sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T09:37:37-08:00","id":793147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=793081#post793081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think those are all reasonable suggestions. This whole thread has got me thinking aboout merits that modify the intrinsic capabilities of demons especially their demonic forms. Maybe there could be one that could allow the demon to use more aether per turn in demonic form? Stuff like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am trying to think of something that's based off of mechanics in Leviathan: The Tempest, specifically where a Leviathan can spend up to two points in excess of his Sheol limits at the risk of experiencing an Outburst. Maybe something similar could be made for Unchained?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=793089#post793089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was trying to figure out a system of allowing Demons to boost their Attributes. I figured letting them &quot;use&quot; their form abilities on a one-for-one basis (which would prevent usage of those abilities, and cap the total bonus).</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you elaborate more on this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T10:03:15-08:00","id":793166,"title":"","content":"DELETED POST","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","user":"lladas","date":". 12-26-2015, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T10:03:56-08:00","id":793167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=793147#post793147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am trying to think of something that's based off of mechanics in Leviathan: The Tempest, specifically where a Leviathan can spend up to two points in excess of his Sheol limits at the risk of experiencing an Outburst. Maybe something similar could be made for Unchained?</div> </div> </div> </div>Knowing that system I think I see what you are going for. The merit could work the same for Unchained, but instead of Outburst you could come up with a new condition that would work. Thinking about when in my chronicles I have wanted something like this, combat resoundingly comes to mind which I think could inform the drawback. I don't think a compromise check would make sense. Perhaps the condition would limit the time the Unchained can be in demonic form as they push themself?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T10:11:14-08:00","id":793171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=793167#post793167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Knowing that system I think I see what you are going for. The merit could work the same for Unchained, but instead of Outburst you could come up with a new condition that would work. Thinking about when in my chronicles I have wanted something like this, combat resoundingly comes to mind which I think could inform the drawback. I don't think a compromise check would make sense. Perhaps the condition would limit the time the Unchained can be in demonic form as they push themself?</div> </div> </div> </div>If we went by existing Conditions, perhaps Aetheric Bleed might work?<br /> <br /> P.S: Is it possible for you to delete the buggy version of your most recent reply?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T10:28:11-08:00","id":793179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=793171#post793171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If we went by existing Conditions, perhaps Aetheric Bleed might work?{\\</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that you make sense thematically and mechanically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=793171#post793171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">P.S: Is it possible for you to delete the buggy version of your most recent reply?</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally would if they hadn't removed the delete button from the edit option.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T10:32:27-08:00","id":793181,"title":"","content":"Figures...<br /> <br /> Maybe you could just edit that first one and say &quot;DELETED&quot;? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, for a name for that Merit, how does &quot;Overload&quot; sound?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T10:50:34-08:00","id":793192,"title":"","content":"So I went with DELETED and was notified that it has to be ten characters so for future reference &quot;DELETED POST&quot; is ten characters.<br /> <br /> That sounds good. Have you thought about what kind of prerequisites if any you would have for the merit? How about dot cost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T18:29:36-08:00","id":793362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=793147#post793147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you elaborate more on this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I was on my phone.<br /> <br /> Basically, the idea was to allow a Demon to do a special Partial Transformation, but instead of manifesting the specific Form ability, they instead get a +1 [Attribute]. Since it is still a Partial Transformation, it is still subject to all those limitations (costs Aether, risks Compromise, need to revert to &quot;normal&quot; before additional Transformations, etc.). Since it is &quot;using&quot; the Form ability, you are trading off the option of what it could do for a generic bonus. The Attribute booster abilities are also still competetive/more efficient.<br /> <br /> I was mostly trying to decide whether to have it as a straight bonus attribute pool (simpler), or serve as an attribute replacement (meaning you' need to convert X+1 Form abilities, where X is the Attribute in question, to see any real improvement - that would greatly limit the ability to exceed normal Attribute limits).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T19:36:05-08:00","id":793382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=793192#post793192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I went with DELETED and was notified that it has to be ten characters so for future reference &quot;DELETED POST&quot; is ten characters.<br /> <br /> That sounds good. Have you thought about what kind of prerequisites if any you would have for the merit? How about dot cost?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I got so far...<br /> <br /> <b><u>Overdrive</u> (o to ooooo)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Resolve 3 or Composure 3<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You have learned to vent out more power than is normally possible within the limits of your Aetheric Soul. While this comes with certain dangers, it nonetheless grants you a trump card against many of the God-Machine's agents. For each dot in this Merit, you can spend one point of Aether in a turn above the maximum imposed by your Primum.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Each time you use Overdrive, you must roll Resolve + Composure at a penalty equal to the number of Aether spent beyond your normal limits. On a failure, you gain the Aetheric Bleed Condition, and must make a Glitch roll with a dice bonus equal to the excess Aether.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=793362#post793362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, I was on my phone.<br /> <br /> Basically, the idea was to allow a Demon to do a special Partial Transformation, but instead of manifesting the specific Form ability, they instead get a +1 [Attribute]. Since it is still a Partial Transformation, it is still subject to all those limitations (costs Aether, risks Compromise, need to revert to &quot;normal&quot; before additional Transformations, etc.). Since it is &quot;using&quot; the Form ability, you are trading off the option of what it could do for a generic bonus. The Attribute booster abilities are also still competetive/more efficient.<br /> <br /> I was mostly trying to decide whether to have it as a straight bonus attribute pool (simpler), or serve as an attribute replacement (meaning you' need to convert X+1 Form abilities, where X is the Attribute in question, to see any real improvement - that would greatly limit the ability to exceed normal Attribute limits).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm.<br /> <br /> This seems to be a bit too convoluted for my taste. I'd personally still prefer the Inhuman Attribute Modifications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 12-27-2015, 12:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T04:16:25-08:00","id":793502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=793382#post793382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is what I got so far...<br /> <br /> <b><u>Overdrive</u> (o to ooooo)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Resolve 3 or Composure 3<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You have learned to vent out more power than is normally possible within the limits of your Aetheric Soul. While this comes with certain dangers, it nonetheless grants you a trump card against many of the God-Machine's agents. For each dot in this Merit, you can spend one point of Aether in a turn above the maximum imposed by your Primum.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Each time you use Overdrive, you must roll Resolve + Composure at a penalty equal to the number of Aether spent beyond your normal limits. On a failure, you gain the Aetheric Bleed Condition, and must make a Glitch roll with a dice bonus equal to the excess Aether.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely like it and can see where some of my more aether hungry players would like this in our current chronicle. My only concern would be in players building around this to circumnavigate the drawback and using this every combat, but that is only something that comes with testing.I suppose.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T04:44:05-08:00","id":793513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=793502#post793502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definitely like it and can see where some of my more aether hungry players would like this in our current chronicle. My only concern would be in players building around this to circumnavigate the drawback and using this every combat, but that is only something that comes with testing.I suppose.</div> </div> </div> </div>If ever, you could raise the Attribute requirement for the Merit so that it could be something that isn't lightly invested, but nonetheless can be rewarding if built right.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you could up the drawback by including lethal damage,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T04:49:45-08:00","id":793515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=793513#post793513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If ever, you could raise the Attribute requirement for the Merit so that it could be something that isn't lightly invested, but nonetheless can be rewarding if built right.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you could up the drawback by including lethal damage,</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or applying a penalty against the drawback roll for each time it is used (1st time's free, then -1, etc.). Still useful, but makes it harder to abuse throughout the scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T04:59:07-08:00","id":793519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=793515#post793515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or applying a penalty against the drawback roll for each time it is used (1st time's free, then -1, etc.). Still useful, but makes it harder to abuse throughout the scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>That actually can work. It shows that the more (and longer) you force yourself beyond your limits, the more prone you are to disaster.<br /> <br /> To expand on this, once the penalty reaches -5, all failures should be treated as dramatic failures in subsequent uses. And the dramatic failure can take the form of lethal (or even aggravated) damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T06:00:49-08:00","id":793535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=793519#post793519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That actually can work. It shows that the more (and longer) you force yourself beyond your limits, the more prone you are to disaster.<br /> <br /> To expand on this, once the penalty reaches -5, all failures should be treated as dramatic failures in subsequent uses. And the dramatic failure can take the form of lethal (or even aggravated) damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>This could definitely work and would be thematically interesting. Would you still keep the drawback for the multiple points in the merit? Otherwise, there wouldn't really be a reason to not get the higher one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T06:10:45-08:00","id":793536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=793535#post793535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This could definitely work and would be thematically interesting. Would you still keep the drawback for the multiple points in the merit? Otherwise, there wouldn't really be a reason to not get the higher one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would. The higher version allows for the option of more power when necessary - even while it gives the Demon more rope with which to hang themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T06:14:16-08:00","id":793537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=793535#post793535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This could definitely work and would be thematically interesting. Would you still keep the drawback for the multiple points in the merit? Otherwise, there wouldn't really be a reason to not get the higher one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd agree with Vent on his points.<br /> <br /> If ever, though, I would probably at least retain the bit where the glitch roll gets a bonus equal to the extra Aether you can spend. Since that would still give a reason for Unchained to avoid abusing Overdrive in the event of a failed Resolve + Composure roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 12-27-2015, 09:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T06:51:37-08:00","id":793548,"title":"","content":"Sounds good. I'll probably use this soon enough.<br /> <br /> Has anyone ever heard of a Bolthole aspect that works like Arsenal, but can be used for equipment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T07:58:36-08:00","id":794185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=793548#post793548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds good. I'll probably use this soon enough.<br /> <br /> Has anyone ever heard of a Bolthole aspect that works like Arsenal, but can be used for equipment?</div> </div> </div> </div>By equipment, are you meaning armor and/or utility gadgets? You might want to clarify for me, there. But either way, I'd say there isn't an existing Bolthole aspect for that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T10:20:41-08:00","id":794250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=794185#post794185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By equipment, are you meaning armor and/or utility gadgets? You might want to clarify for me, there. But either way, I'd say there isn't an existing Bolthole aspect for that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry about that. I meant along the lines of equipment like computers, cell phones, climbing gear, etc. Stuff that would add a bonus to a skill roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T17:22:05-08:00","id":794487,"title":"","content":"Right. Then, no. There isn't any existing Aspect like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T17:47:50-08:00","id":794497,"title":"","content":"Reposting this, again, with the recommended additions.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Overdrive</u> (o to ooooo)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Resolve 3 or Composure 3<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You have learned to vent out more power than is normally possible within the limits of your Aetheric Soul. While this comes with certain dangers, it nonetheless grants you a trump card against many of the God-Machine's agents. For each dot in this Merit, you can spend one point of Aether in a turn above the maximum imposed by your Primum.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Whenever you use Overdrive, you must roll Resolve + Composure at a penalty equal to the number of Aether spent beyond your normal limits. On a failure, you gain the Aetheric Bleed Condition, and must make a Glitch roll with a dice bonus equal to the excess Aether. On a dramatic failure, you take lethal damage equal to successes in the Glitch roll. Subsequent uses of Overdrive after the first within the same scene confer an additional -1 penalty (which maxes out at -5). After reaching -5, treat all failures in the Overdrive roll as dramatic failures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T07:03:41-08:00","id":794799,"title":"","content":"Another new Merit. One that will probably appeal very well to the Saboteurs. Additionally, I think this warrants a very apt flavor text. <hr /><br /> <i>&quot;If we burn, you burn with us!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b><u>Outburst</u> (ooo)<br /> Effect:</b> Maybe you've been through it more often than you care to admit. Or maybe your Primum burns more fiercely than it ever had before. But whenever you go loud, you can do so like an exploding sun. You can opt to unleash an explosion with a radius of 10 yards in place in place of rolling for a transient glitch if you choose to go loud. This explosion inflicts the Demon's temporary Primum - as well as any successes in a Primum roll (10) - as direct lethal damage on all targets within the blast radius.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback: </b>Such a show of destruction can cause the 'human' side of the Unchained to snap. After going loud, roll Resolve + Composure. On a success, he simply suffers the Demonic Rage Condition. On a failure, he also takes the Demonic Disconnect Condition, which persists even after he's reverted to human form for a number of scenes equal to his Primum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 12-29-2015, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T07:24:52-08:00","id":794814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=791059#post791059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Advanced Self-Repair System 3 Dots</u></b><br /> <b>Perquisite: </b>Terrible Form (Style) 2 Dots<br /> The demons ability to heal between transformations is supported by a more advanced internal system. While transitioning into Full Transformation, the demon can spend aether to downgrade aggravated damage to lethal at a one-to-one cost. In Partial Transformation, the demon heals one extra box of health.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also taking into consideration the suggestions I proposed to you, good sir.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b><u>Advanced Self Repair System</u> (ooo or ooooo)</b><br /> <b>Perquisite: </b>Terrible Form oo<br /> <b>Effect: </b>The Demon's ability to heal between transformations is supported by a more advanced internal system. How efficient this system is depends on the Merit's dot rating.<br /> <br /> For the three-dot version, while performing a Full Transformation, the Demon can spend Aether to downgrade aggravated damage to lethal at a one-to-one cost. In a Partial Transformation, the Demon heals bashing and lethal damage equal to half its Primum, rounded down (to minimum of 1).<br /> <br /> For the five-dot version, while performing a Full Transformation, the Demon can heal one point of aggravated damage for every two dots of Primum. In a Partial Transformation, it can heal an amount of bashing and lethal damage equal to its Primum, and can apply the three-dot version of the Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 12-29-2015, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T07:44:56-08:00","id":794822,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Embed Affinity</b></u><b> \u2022\u2022\u2022</b> (maybe \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 ?)<br /> <b>Effect</b>: The Demon gets a +1 bonus to rolls with Embeds in the category associated with their Incarnation.<br /> <br /> <u>Notes:</u> Merit form of a house-rule I have to enforce those Incarnation Embed affinities. The +1 is effectively equivalent to a Specialization (and as such, only makes them 33% more efficient than their peers in that category). Sadly leaves Analysts out in the cold. <hr /><br /> And now some fun for Stigmatics...<br /> <br /> <b><u>Cohabitation</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite</b>: Sleeve Integrator<br /> <b>Effect</b>: When allowing a Demon to take your identity as a Cover, your mind remains &quot;awake&quot;, allowing you to remain aware of events and communicate with the Demon (such as offering up critical information to maintain the charade).<br /> <br /> <b><u>Quantum Synthesis</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite</b>: Cohabitation<br /> <b>Effect</b>: When serving as a Cover, you can let the Demon use your Attributes and/or Skills instead of theirs, if they are better.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Usurp Control</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> Prerequisite</b>: Cohabitation<br /> <b>Effect</b>: While being used as a Cover, as a Reflexive action once per scene you can contest control by spending one Willpower point and making a Resolve + Composure roll penalized by the Demon's Resolve + Primum.<ul><li><u>Dramatic Failure</u>: Not only do you fail in the attempt, you alert the Demon to your efforts and have your awareness turned &quot;off&quot; for the duration of the Integration. Few Unchained are likely to treat your identity very kindly after such an action.</li> <li><u>Failure</u>: Your efforts to take control failed, and the Demon makes a Wits + Composure roll penalized by your Stealth [or Manipulation?] to notice the attempt.</li> <li><u>Success</u>: You take control of your identity for the remainder of the merge using the Demon's abilities as if they were your own.</li> <li><u>Exceptional Success</u>: Not only do you take control, you manage to black-out the Demon's awareness. You still may need to come up with a convincing lie regarding what happened.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Drawback</b>: Any Stigmatic caught doing this is going to incur a <i>very</i> bad reputation amongst the Unchained.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Poison Pill</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite</b>: Sleeve Integrator<br /> <b>Effect</b>: After the merger ends, you may transfer any Conditions and damage you were suffering before it to the Demon. Further more, the Demon cannot Go Loud while using your identity as a Cover.<br /> <b>Drawback</b>: Doing this without previous agreement from the Unchained in question is a good way to have a powerful entity pissed off at you.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Hollow Vessel</u> \u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite</b>: Sleeve Integrator<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You have a great void inside you that only seems to abate when you are connected to demonic Primum. This void is not only a psychological hunger, but can also draw in unwary Demons as well. You may touch one of the Unchained as an Instant action and spend a point of Willpower to force the Demon to take you as a Cover (as per Sleeve Integrator), even if the Demon can no longer maintain any more Covers.<br /> <b>Drawback</b>: After 1 week without serving as a Cover, you gain the Addicted Condition keyed to being used as a Cover again.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Aether Syphon</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite</b>: Cohabitation<br /> <b>Effect</b>: You can a special Aether pool equal to your Stamina. Whenever you end a merge, in addition to selecting Embeds, you may also drain enough Aether from the Demon to fill up this Aether pool. You can spend the Aether on supercharging Embeds (see Heirs to Hell, page xx) or for other applicable purposes.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Exploit Capacitor</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Cohabitation, Aether Syphon<br /> <b>Effect</b>: After ending a merge, you can also store one Exploit that the Demon knows, provided that you also select one of its prerequisite Embeds. You can use this Exploit <i>once</i> (until another merger), as if you had Primum 1, and doing so always provokes a check against Integrity (with any penalties to a Compromise roll also penalizing this roll).<br /> <b>Drawback</b>: Even holding this spark of demonic power is dangerous and debilitating. Roll to acquire a temporary Glitch, which lasts until the Embed is used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 12-29-2015, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T08:33:34-08:00","id":794846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=794814#post794814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also taking into consideration the suggestions I proposed to you, good sir.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b><u>Advanced Self Repair System</u> (ooo or ooooo)</b><br /> <b>Perquisite: </b>Terrible Form oo<br /> <b>Effect: </b>The Demon's ability to heal between transformations is supported by a more advanced internal system. How efficient this system is depends on the Merit's dot rating.<br /> <br /> For the three-dot version, while performing a Full Transformation, the Demon can spend Aether to downgrade aggravated damage to lethal at a one-to-one cost. In a Partial Transformation, the Demon heals bashing and lethal damage equal to half its Primum, rounded down (to minimum of 1).<br /> <br /> For the five-dot version, while performing a Full Transformation, the Demon can heal one point of aggravated damage for every two dots of Primum. In a Partial Transformation, it can heal an amount of bashing and lethal damage equal to its Primum, and can apply the three-dot version of the Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much. I completely forgot about that. I am definitely going to test that out with an NPC Unchained and see how hard it is to kill. <br /> <br /> What do you think about this?<br /> <br /> <b><u>Equipment</u></b> (o to ooooo)<br /> <b>Effect: </b>Your bolthole stores a metaphysical collection of mundane equipment for you to use once per session. One item with a skill bonus equal to dots spent in equipment, two items with bonuses of Equipment-1, and an infinite amount of items at Equipment-2. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T08:34:57-08:00","id":794849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=794822#post794822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Embed Affinity</b></u><b> \u2022\u2022\u2022</b> (maybe \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 ?)<br /> <b>Effect</b>: The Demon gets a +1 bonus to rolls with Embeds in the category associated with their Incarnation.<br /> <hr /><br /> Merit form of a house-rule I have to enforce those Incarnation Embed affinities. The +1 is effectively equivalent to a Specialization (and as such, only makes them 33% more efficient than their peers in that category). Sadly leaves Analysts out in the cold.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you thought about possibly allowing the Affinity to be with what ever type of Embed the Unchained want?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T08:49:54-08:00","id":794861,"title":"","content":"(I'll delete or move this is desired - it is kind of off topic)<br /> <br /> Now I'm getting an idea for a plot and related Template based off the end state of this chain of merits - a Demon-Eater. Basically, instead of merely usurping control, the Stigmatic (now human-Cryptid?) <i>consumes</i> the Unchained within, adding their Embeds, Aether, and Primum to a growing collection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T08:53:03-08:00","id":794863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=794849#post794849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you thought about possibly allowing the Affinity to be with what ever type of Embed the Unchained want?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could, I guess. The point was really a mechanical representation of the Incarnation -&gt; Embed category fluff.<br /> <br /> Should I reposition the new Stigmatic merits I added to the post above, or did people notice them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T08:55:54-08:00","id":794865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=794861#post794861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I'll delete or move this is desired - it is kind of off topic)<br /> <br /> Now I'm getting an idea for a plot and related Template based off the end state of this chain of merits - a Demon-Eater. Basically, instead of merely usurping control, the Stigmatic (now human-Cryptid?) <i>consumes</i> the Unchained within, adding their Embeds, Aether, and Primum to a growing collection.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could definitely see this. The old Demon the Fallen fiction had a story that was pretty much this. Perhaps the powers consumed this way can only stay in the target for so long forcing the eater to continue to hunt to feed their addiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T10:20:58-08:00","id":794918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=794846#post794846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you very much. I completely forgot about that. I am definitely going to test that out with an NPC Unchained and see how hard it is to kill.<br /> <br /> What do you think about this?<br /> <br /> <b><u>Equipment</u></b> (o to ooooo)<br /> <b>Effect: </b>Your bolthole stores a metaphysical collection of mundane equipment for you to use once per session. One item with a skill bonus equal to dots spent in equipment, two items with bonuses of Equipment-1, and an infinite amount of items at Equipment-2.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sweet. Let me know how that goes down, if you can.<br /> :3<br /> <br /> And that Equipment aspect seems good. It could probably do well in filling a niche for utility items.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts on Outburst, though?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=794822#post794822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b><u>Cohabitation</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite</b>: Sleeve Integrator<br /> <b>Effect</b>: When allowing a Demon to take your identity as a Cover, your mind remains &quot;awake&quot;, allowing you to remain aware of events and communicate with the Demon (such as offering up critical information to maintain the charade).<br /> <br /> <b><u>Quantum Synthesis</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite</b>: Cohabitation<br /> <b>Effect</b>: When serving as a Cover, you can let the Demon use your Attributes and/or Skills instead of theirs, if they are better.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Usurp Control</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> Prerequisite</b>: Cohabitation<br /> <b>Effect</b>: While being used as a Cover, as a Reflexive action once per scene you can contest control by spending one Willpower point and making a Resolve + Composure roll penalized by the Demon's Resolve + Primum.<ul><li><u>Dramatic Failure</u>: Not only do you fail in the attempt, you alert the Demon to your efforts and have your awareness turned &quot;off&quot; for the duration of the Integration. Few Unchained are likely to treat your identity very kindly after such an action.</li> <li><u>Failure</u>: Your efforts to take control failed, and the Demon makes a Wits + Composure roll penalized by your Stealth [or Manipulation?] to notice the attempt.</li> <li><u>Success</u>: You take control of your identity for the remainder of the merge using the Demon's abilities as if they were your own.</li> <li><u>Exceptional Success</u>: Not only do you take control, you manage to black-out the Demon's awareness. You still may need to come up with a convincing lie regarding what happened.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Drawback</b>: Any Stigmatic caught doing this is going to incur a <i>very</i> bad reputation amongst the Unchained.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Poison Pill</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite</b>: Sleeve Integrator<br /> <b>Effect</b>: After the merger ends, you may transfer any Conditions and damage you were suffering before it to the Demon. Further more, the Demon cannot Go Loud while using your identity as a Cover.<br /> <b>Drawback</b>: Doing this without previous agreement from the Unchained in question is a good way to have a powerful entity pissed off at you.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Hollow Vessel</u> \u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite</b>: Sleeve Integrator<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You have a great void inside you that only seems to abate when you are connected to demonic Primum. This void is not only a psychological hunger, but can also draw in unwary Demons as well. You may touch one of the Unchained as an Instant action and spend a point of Willpower to force the Demon to take you as a Cover (as per Sleeve Integrator), even if the Demon can no longer maintain any more Covers.<br /> <b>Drawback</b>: After 1 week without serving as a Cover, you gain the Addicted Condition keyed to being used as a Cover again.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Aether Syphon</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite</b>: Cohabitation<br /> <b>Effect</b>: You can a special Aether pool equal to your Stamina. Whenever you end a merge, in addition to selecting Embeds, you may also drain enough Aether from the Demon to fill up this Aether pool. You can spend the Aether on supercharging Embeds (see Heirs to Hell, page xx) or for other applicable purposes.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Exploit Capacitor</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Cohabitation, Aether Syphon<br /> <b>Effect</b>: After ending a merge, you can also store one Exploit that the Demon knows, provided that you also select one of its prerequisite Embeds. You can use this Exploit <i>once</i> (until another merger), as if you had Primum 1, and doing so always provokes a check against Integrity (with any penalties to a Compromise roll also penalizing this roll).<br /> <b>Drawback</b>: Even holding this spark of demonic power is dangerous and debilitating. Roll to acquire a temporary Glitch, which lasts until the Embed is used.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, these are some pretty awesome Merits for Stigmatics here. One question, though. Would it make sense for a Demon-Blooded character to have Aether Syphon AND Aether Pool together? <br /> <br /> But other than that, I'm really liking them. Especially the ones that can make a Stigmatic a body snatcher (or, in this case, a Demon Snatcher). Heck, if you had Stigmatics like that siding with the God Machine, I can see them acting as the perfect honey traps for Unchained.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T10:51:48-08:00","id":794945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=794918#post794918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sweet. Let me know how that goes down, if you can.<br /> :3<br /> <br /> And that Equipment aspect seems good. It could probably do well in filling a niche for utility items.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts on Outburst, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry I missed this completely. I definitely like this a lot and can see its utility. I like the effect of it as is. It's powerful, indiscriminate, and is more manageable than the Self Destruct mechanic introduced in Interface. I guess I only have two questions: First, does this feel more like a merit, or, more like something all demons can do? Secondly, the drawbacks make sense, but I was wondering how you would feel about possibly tacking something on that played into the theme of letting loose with all that energy? Something like what you see in the latest (albeit mixed) run with Superman. They could have a condition that leaves their primiuim one less than where it was before they went loud and can only beat it by buying the next level of primium. The only reason I suggest this is that I can imagine this being used to clear out some serious angelic/supernatural threats with one shot. I hope that all makes sense.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T10:53:54-08:00","id":794947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=794918#post794918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, these are some pretty awesome Merits for Stigmatics here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. :-)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=794918#post794918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One question, though. Would it make sense for a Demon-Blooded character to have Aether Syphon AND Aether Pool together?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe? The possibility of such is why I declared the Aether pool for Aether Syphon to be special/separate. Sleeve Integrator is far more attractive to non-Demon-Blooded Stigmatics, since it is (currently) the only way for them to gain access to Embeds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=794918#post794918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But other than that, I'm really liking them. Especially the ones that can make a Stigmatic a body snatcher (or, in this case, a Demon Snatcher). Heck, if you had Stigmatics like that siding with the God Machine, I can see them acting as the perfect honey traps for Unchained.</div> </div> </div> </div>These actually arose from a plot idea I had: some G-M Project or Infrastructure was able to detect Demons in normal Cover after a day (or prevent them from maintaining a Cover for more than a day), forcing the Unchained in the city to work with Sleeve Integrator Stigmatics. Then I created an entire organization (Agency?) of Stigmatics that &quot;loaned out&quot; themselves. Then I wanted more mechanical support and incentives (because the Embeds at the end are nice, but you are essentially giving the Demon a blank check to your life for a day).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T10:56:59-08:00","id":794948,"title":"","content":"Vent0! Those merits are terrifying and wonderful. They move Stigmatics and Demon-Blooded from useful characters to useful/deceptive antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T11:14:48-08:00","id":794965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=794948#post794948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vent0! Those merits are terrifying and wonderful. They move Stigmatics and Demon-Blooded from useful characters to useful/deceptive antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.<br /> <br /> Technically, even if a Stigmatic possessed all of the merits, they are still an attractive option for Demons to &quot;use&quot; as a Cover - Cohabitation means you need never stumble over characterization or missing information when the person you are imitating is <i>right there</i> to tell it to you. Quantum Synthesis reduces/eliminates the need for Legend, since your &quot;co-pilot&quot; can take control as needed. Exploit Capacitor lets them perform a potentially needed burst of power afterwards (and, if combined with the Gadgeteer merit from before, allows them to Install Exploits into Gadgets). The other merits simply serve as insurance that you don't screw the Stigmatic over. They don't <i>have</i> to invoke any of the detrimental effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T11:21:29-08:00","id":794968,"title":"","content":"Related plot/merit idea:<br /> <br /> Would the ability to &quot;migrate&quot; a Stigmatic's soul/identity/mind from Cover (their identity as a Cover via Sleeve Integrator) to a different Cover the Demon possesses be a merit, or more of a story power/ability? Because a person trading in their &quot;old&quot; life for a new one the Unchained constructs (a new Patch job or Soul Pact) is really only missing that one step at this stage. <hr /><br /> As a merit (<i>highly</i> theoretical and rough at this point):<br /> <br /> <b><u>Identity Swap</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite</b>: Sleeve Integrator (or Cohabitation?)<br /> <b>Effect</b>: The character now has an additional option when forming a Pact with one of the Unchained - when their life/identity is taken as a Cover (via Sleeve Integrator), they can &quot;sign off&quot; on their claim to that life and trade it for another Cover the Demon possesses. The Pact processes is resolved as normal, but when the Stigmatic opens themselves up for use as a Cover, they must spend one Willpower <b>dot</b> instead of a point. The Sleeve Integration merger is likewise normal, but at the end the Stigmatic is separated from the Demon into the agreed upon Cover instead of their old one.<br /> <br /> [Note: As far as the Demon end is concerned, this is a Soul Pact, except the signer pays the Willpower Dot, and get the benefit of [Cover] worth +3, which cancels out the Demon's +3 for the Soul Pact.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-06-2016, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T13:34:37-08:00","id":795050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=794968#post794968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Related plot/merit idea:<br /> <br /> Would the ability to &quot;migrate&quot; a Stigmatic's soul/identity/mind from Cover (their identity as a Cover via Sleeve Integrator) to a different Cover the Demon possesses be a merit, or more of a story power/ability? Because a person trading in their &quot;old&quot; life for a new one the Unchained constructs (a new Patch job or Soul Pact) is really only missing that one step at this stage.<br /> <hr /><br /> As a merit (<i>highly</i> theoretical and rough at this point):<br /> <br /> <b><u>Identity Swap</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite</b>: Sleeve Integrator (or Cohabitation?)<br /> <b>Effect</b>: The character now has an additional option when forming a Pact with one of the Unchained - when their life/identity is taken as a Cover (via Sleeve Integrator), they can &quot;sign off&quot; on their claim to that life and trade it for another Cover the Demon possesses. The Pact processes is resolved as normal, but when the Stigmatic opens themselves up for use as a Cover, they must spend one Willpower <b>dot</b> instead of a point. The Sleeve Integration merger is likewise normal, but at the end the Stigmatic is separated from the Demon into the agreed upon Cover instead of their old one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely like the flavor of the merit and I can see where this could work in the story, but I am not sure if this situation would come up enough for it to be a merit instead of just a story piece. The only reason I say that is because I am not sure how often in a chronicle you will have a demon who trusts a person enough to let them play in a Cover while they use their identity. Even if a demon does trust someone that much that person would have to be able to do this. What could be interesting and more accessible is a merit where a Sleeve Integrator could jump into one of the Unchained's Cover without the Unchained knowing. Or you could add a new aspect to soul pacts where an individual could bargain to jump into another soul pact if that makes any sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T13:46:37-08:00","id":795054,"title":"","content":"I have a player who just recently lost their character and so she wanted to make an Uncalled Unchained, but after looking it over she didn\u2019t really understand mechanically why if all she got for it was a loss of options. This got me thinking about a possible merit:<br /> <br /> <b><u>Mercenary</u></b> (oo)<br /> <b>Perquisite: </b>Uncalled, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Effect: </b>Amongst the Unchained community, you have a reputation for being skilled at what you do, willing to work for a price, and above all else discrete about your employer. You receive a +2 bonus to any relevant Social roll when negotiating a deal for your services.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T13:51:32-08:00","id":795056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=795050#post795050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I definitely like the flavor of the merit and I can see where this could work in the story, but I am not sure if this situation would come up enough for it to be a merit instead of just a story piece. The only reason I say that is because I am not sure how often in a chronicle you will have a demon who trusts a person enough to let them play in a Cover while they use their identity. Even if a demon does trust someone that much that person would have to be able to do this. What could be interesting and more accessible is a merit where a Sleeve Integrator could jump into one of the Unchained's Cover without the Unchained knowing. Or you could add a new aspect to soul pacts where an individual could bargain to jump into another soul pact if that makes any sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, point of clarification, the Stigmatic doesn't get to &quot;play&quot; in one of the Demon's Cover's while the Demon uses their identity - the Stigmatic is <i>trading</i> their identity in for the Cover. At the end of the transaction, the Demon is down one Cover and up another (essentially a Soul Pact), while the Stigmatic has a whole new identity (that of the discarded/traded Cover). The Demon need never interact with that Cover (now a real person) again. Not sure if that changes your read on it.<br /> <br /> And yes, nothing is stopping a Demon from trading out attractive seeming &quot;damaged goods&quot; (like a Cover that has warrants pending, or is being investigated by Angels). Buyer Beware.<br /> <br /> Of course, in theme with the previous merits, one could be developed that allows the Stigmatic to &quot;force the issue&quot; as it were. I'n not sure how much alteration a person would have to undergo to be able to switch between two &quot;real&quot; identities, though. At that point I doubt they are a mortal with some supernatural about them, but more of a supernatural <i>thing</i> at that point (a human-Cryptid).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T14:04:09-08:00","id":795064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=795056#post795056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, point of clarification, the Stigmatic doesn't get to &quot;play&quot; in one of the Demon's Cover's while the Demon uses their identity - the Stigmatic is <i>trading</i> their identity in for the Cover. At the end of the transaction, the Demon is down one Cover and up another (essentially a Soul Pact), while the Stigmatic has a whole new identity (that of the discarded/traded Cover). The Demon need never interact with that Cover (now a real person) again. Not sure if that changes your read on it.<br /> <br /> And yes, nothing is stopping a Demon from trading out attractive seeming &quot;damaged goods&quot; (like a Cover that has warrants pending, or is being investigated by Angels). Buyer Beware.<br /> <br /> Of course, in theme with the previous merits, one could be developed that allows the Stigmatic to &quot;force the issue&quot; as it were. I'n not sure how much alteration a person would have to undergo to be able to switch between two &quot;real&quot; identities, though. At that point I doubt they are a mortal with some supernatural about them, but more of a supernatural <i>thing</i> at that point (a human-Cryptid).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think with that clarification then I think your merit would be solid as is honestly. I think clarifying on where the person becomes that pervious cover would be useful. Something along the lines of &quot;The Stigmatic appears in the last place the Unchained was in the Cover.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T22:29:03-08:00","id":795400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=794945#post794945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry I missed this completely. I definitely like this a lot and can see its utility. I like the effect of it as is. It's powerful, indiscriminate, and is more manageable than the Self Destruct mechanic introduced in Interface. I guess I only have two questions: First, does this feel more like a merit, or, more like something all demons can do? Secondly, the drawbacks make sense, but I was wondering how you would feel about possibly tacking something on that played into the theme of letting loose with all that energy? Something like what you see in the latest (albeit mixed) run with Superman. They could have a condition that leaves their primiuim one less than where it was before they went loud and can only beat it by buying the next level of primium. The only reason I suggest this is that I can imagine this being used to clear out some serious angelic/supernatural threats with one shot. I hope that all makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. I think I get the point you're trying to get across.<br /> <br /> The reason I put it as a Merit was because I imagine going loud in this manner to be something that needs to be learned. Even without a Cover, perhaps the Primum of a Demon is still influenced by instinctive protocols to contain the bulk of such a burst of power within its body. This also may explain the Glitch roll, as the Demon's body has difficulty processing all that power in itself. That said, I justified Outburst as a Merit by saying that the Unchained has circumvented those 'safeties' (I should probably revise the write-up of Outburst to reflect that).<br /> <br /> On a related note, perhaps Outburst is not easy to pull off compared to the 'usual' style of going loud. Perhaps a Willpower point and/or Resolve + Composure roll would be required? That would fit for whether or not it's a Merit, or a House-Ruled addition to the template itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T05:52:06-08:00","id":796791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=795064#post795064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think with that clarification then I think your merit would be solid as is honestly. I think clarifying on where the person becomes that pervious cover would be useful. Something along the lines of &quot;The Stigmatic appears in the last place the Unchained was in the Cover.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, it is intended to work like Sleeve Integrator normally does (you and the Demon separate at the end of the 1 day duration), but with you leaving with the Demon's other Cover, rather than your own. And since Demons are all there Covers at once, the last place the Cover would technically be is where the Demon is. Plus, it would otherwise lead to weird scenarios like a person popping into existence who knows where (seriously, what if the Demon swaped out of that Cover while on a plane bathroom - would you appear in that bathroom, regardless of its occupancy, or in mid air where the change occurred? Too tricky to mediate).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T12:48:34-08:00","id":796968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=795400#post795400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On a related note, perhaps Outburst is not easy to pull off compared to the 'usual' style of going loud. Perhaps a Willpower point and/or Resolve + Composure roll would be required? That would fit for whether or not it's a Merit, or a House-Ruled addition to the template itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that definitely takes into the realm of a Merit. What are your thoughts on prerequisites? I don't think you would need to do both a roll and a WP point. Maybe just make the cost aether and keep the roll. The successes can determine if the Unchained gets injured on a failure or can direct the damage on an exceptional success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T12:50:30-08:00","id":796972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=796791#post796791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, it is intended to work like Sleeve Integrator normally does (you and the Demon separate at the end of the 1 day duration), but with you leaving with the Demon's other Cover, rather than your own. And since Demons are all there Covers at once, the last place the Cover would technically be is where the Demon is. Plus, it would otherwise lead to weird scenarios like a person popping into existence who knows where (seriously, what if the Demon swaped out of that Cover while on a plane bathroom - would you appear in that bathroom, regardless of its occupancy, or in mid air where the change occurred? Too tricky to mediate).</div> </div> </div> </div>I see what you are saying and I can see the problem with my suggestion. I think it's a solid addition to the list that you have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T12:19:37-08:00","id":802261,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Snitch</u> \u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Demon, having a Cover<br /> <b>Effects</b>: The God-Machine has some way to detect when a human witnesses Demonic activity or the irregular circumstances of a Demon's Cover. You've figured out how to spoof the same signal. When in Cover as a mortal, you may opt to turn on or off this &quot;notification&quot; and count as a mortal for the purposes of provoking and exacerbating Compromise checks in your presence.<br /> <b>Drawback</b>: There is a reason for the childhood rhyme &quot;snitches get stitches&quot;. Getting caught doing this is a <i>fabulous</i> way to ruin your goodwill with your fellow Unchained.<br /> [Creator's Notes: This offers up a particularly subtle and dirty way to interfere with other Unchained. If the ST wants, they may even extend the effects to other &quot;viewed by a mortal&quot; supernatural consequences, such as the unraveling effects of Dissonance on a Mage's spells, or the difficulty Ghosts have in Manifesting.]<br /> <br /> <b><u>Pretender</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite</b>: Demon, having a Cover<br /> <b>Effects</b>: You have figured out how to distance yourself from your Cover a bit, letting &quot;it&quot; suffer the effects of a Condition or Tilt. Whenever you would be affected by a Condition or Tilt from a source that does not know you are anything other than a common mortal, and that only affects mortals or has increase effectiveness against mortals, you may pretend to be affected by the Condition/Tilt as a mortal would. At any time, you may &quot;break cover&quot;, removing such Conditions/Tilts immediately at the cost of a Compromise roll penalized by the number of Conditions/Tilts removed in this way.<br /> <b>Drawback</b>: Whenever you cancel Conditions or Tilts your cover was suffering, you get the Cover Disassociation Condition with a number of ticks on it equal to the Conditions and/or Tilts canceled (or add those ticks to the existence Cover Disassociation Condition, if any), tied to the Cover that was used.<br /> [Creator's Notes: An ironclad defense against some powers... provided the conditions are met. A Demon isn't likely to pull off the &quot;just a plain mortal&quot; trick more than once per character, but it is useful for infiltrating supernatural cults and organizations.] <hr /><br /> Condition:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Cover Disassociation</b></u><br /> You feel a disconnect between you and your Cover, leaving you numbed and unable to really empathize with it or other humans. You suffer a -2 penalty to Social rolls while in that Cover due to emotional distance, and a -1 penalty to Mental rolls due to distraction. This Condition is attached with 1 or more ticks. Each day, lower the number of ticks by 1.<br /> <b>Possible Sources</b>: Using Pretender to ignore Conditions or Tilts, some Compromise rolls.<br /> <b>Beat</b>: N/A<br /> <b>Resolution</b>: Reach 0 ticks on this Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-16-2017, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T18:43:22-08:00","id":802528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=802261#post802261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Placeholders for now. I'll fill in the details and edit when I have more time.<br /> <hr /><br /> <b><u>Tattletale</u> \u2022\u2022</b> (change name? Snitch, maybe?)<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Demon, having a Cover<br /> <b>Effects</b>: The God-Machine has some way to detect when a human witnesses Demonic activity or irregular circumstances (such as the holes in a Demon's Cover). You've figured out how to spoof the same signal. When in Cover as a mortal, you may opt to turn on or off this automatic &quot;notification&quot; and count as a mortal for the purposes of provoking and exacerbating Compromise checks in your presence.<br /> <b>Drawback</b>: There is a reason for the childhood rhyme &quot;snitches get stitches&quot;. Getting caught doing this is a <i>fabulous</i> way to ruin your goodwill with your fellow Unchained.<br /> <br /> [Creator's Notes: This offers up a particularly subtle and dirty way to interfere with other Unchained. If the ST wants, they may even extend the effects to other &quot;viewed by a mortal&quot; supernatural consequences, such as the unraveling effects of Dissonance on a Mage's spells, or the difficulty Ghosts have in Manifesting.]</div> </div> </div> </div>Snitch sounds more apt for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T06:42:16-08:00","id":804420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=802261#post802261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Placeholders for now. I'll fill in the details and edit when I have more time.<br /> <hr /><br /> <b><u>Tattletale</u> \u2022\u2022</b> (change name? Snitch, maybe?)<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Demon, having a Cover<br /> <b>Effects</b>: The God-Machine has some way to detect when a human witnesses Demonic activity or irregular circumstances (such as the holes in a Demon's Cover). You've figured out how to spoof the same signal. When in Cover as a mortal, you may opt to turn on or off this automatic &amp;quot;notification&amp;quot; and count as a mortal for the purposes of provoking and exacerbating Compromise checks in your presence.<br /> <b>Drawback</b>: There is a reason for the childhood rhyme &amp;quot;snitches get stitches&amp;quot;. Getting caught doing this is a <i>fabulous</i> way to ruin your goodwill with your fellow Unchained.<br /> [Creator's Notes: This offers up a particularly subtle and dirty way to interfere with other Unchained. If the ST wants, they may even extend the effects to other &amp;quot;viewed by a mortal&amp;quot; supernatural consequences, such as the unraveling effects of Dissonance on a Mage's spells, or the difficulty Ghosts have in Manifesting.]<br /> <br /> <b><u>Pretender</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite</b>: Demon, having a Cover<br /> <b>Effects</b>: You have figured out how to distance yourself from your Cover a bit, letting &amp;quot;it&amp;quot; suffer the effects of a Condition or Tilt. Whenever you would be affected by a Condition or Tilt from a source that does not know you are anything other than a common mortal, and that only affects mortals or has increase effectiveness against mortals, you may pretend to be affected by the Condition/Tilt. At any time, you may &amp;quot;break cover&amp;quot;, removing such Conditions/Tilts immediately at the cost of a Compromise roll penalized by the number of Conditions/Tilts removed in this way.<br /> <b>Drawback</b>: Whenever you cancel Conditions or Tilts your cover was suffering, you get the Cover Disassociation Condition with a number of ticks on it equal to the Conditions and/or Tilts canceled, tied to the Cover that was used.<br /> <hr /><br /> Condition:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Cover Disassociation</b></u><br /> You feel a disconnect between you and your Cover. You suffer a -2 penalty to Social rolls while in that Cover due to emotional distance, and a -1 penalty to Mental rolls due to distraction.<br /> <b>Possible Sources</b>: Using Pretender to ignore Conditions or Tilts, some Compromise rolls. This Condition is attached with 1 or more ticks. Each day, lower the number of ticks by 1.<br /> <b>Beat</b>: N/A<br /> <b>Resolution</b>: Reach 0 ticks on this Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely think snitch is a better choice. Have you ever thought about tying these merits to doffer end agendas? Snitch seems perfect for integrators and pretender would be great for tempters. I only suggest that because I've personally mulled over increasing the mechanical differences between agendas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T14:31:54-08:00","id":804709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=804420#post804420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I definitely think snitch is a better choice. Have you ever thought about tying these merits to doffer end agendas? Snitch seems perfect for integrators and pretender would be great for tempters. I only suggest that because I've personally mulled over increasing the mechanical differences between agendas.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Update: Changed the name, and some of the text.<br /> <br /> While it seems a bit more fitting for Integrators, all Demons should be able to be hypocritical assholes, I feel. Nice, subtle F'ing with your rivals, as they keep glancing over their shoulder looking for spies and witnesses. Might even help maintain <i>your</i> Cover if any Angels are trailing said Demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T05:12:41-08:00","id":805154,"title":"","content":"And now some stuff for Sympathetic Stigmatics and Demons: <hr /><br /> <b><u>Inherent Connection</u> \u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite</b>: Sympathetic Stigmatic or Sympathetic Demon<br /> <b>Effect</b>: The connection with your sympathetic other half is so strong, you can communicate in snippets of images and emotions. You can make a Wits or Intelligence (whichever is higher) + Expression roll as a Reflexive action, up to once per scene. Successes on this roll can convey individual pieces of information, such as descriptions, emotional states, and context between two subjects.<br /> <b>Note</b>: This is a companion Merit to the Inherent Connection possessed by the other half of Sympathetic Stigmatic/Demon.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Summon Demon/Stigmatic</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Inherent Connection, Occult \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Effect</b>: The bond with your sympathetic other half enables you to summon them to you, regardless of distance or complication. Once per scene, either the Demon <i>or</i> the Stigmatic may make a Wits or Intelligence (whichever is higher) + Occult roll penalized by the number of those observing the other character. [Note: I need to add better modifiers, like for the general amount of attention being paid to the target, or the plausibility of escape/travel]<ul><li><u>Dramatic Failure</u>: The connection backlashes, drawing to summoner to the summoned's location.</li> <li><u>Failure</u>: One part fails to summon the other, and must wait until the next scene to attempt again.</li> <li><u>Success</u>: The target is pulled into the presence of the other. They will usually appear in a conveniently unobserved space nearby, but if unavailable, may simply pop into existence out of thin air, provoking Integrity checks and Compromises, as warranted.</li> <li><u>Exceptional Success</u>: The connection is completed so quickly and cleanly, no trace of the relocation remains. The summoned target cannot be traced from where they were, and to all appearances left the area via other means (somehow).</li> </ul><b>Note</b>: If you already possess Sleeve Integrator, whenever you summon your Demon to you, you may opt to activate Sleeve Integrator at the same time. In this case, instead of appearing nearby, the Demon takes your identity as Cover seamlessly, as per Sleeve Integrator.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Second-Hand Skills</u> \u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite</b>: Inherent Connection, Sympathetic Stigmatic<br /> <b>Effect</b>: You can now &quot;borrow&quot; the skills of your Stigmatic. By spending a point of Aether, you can use one of their Skill ratings (if higher than you own) for one scene.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Borrow Legend</u> \u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite</b>: Inherent Connection, Sympathetic Demon<br /> <b>Effect</b>: You can now &quot;borrow&quot; the ability to fake skills from your Demon. By spending a point of Willpower and making a Presence + Subterfuge roll penalized by the desired Skill rating or Merit dots to be emulated, the Stigmatic can use Legend.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Shared Burden</u> \u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite</b>: Sympathetic Stigmatic or Sympathetic Demon<br /> <b>Effect</b>: The tie to your sympathetic other half allows you to transmigrate certain deleterious circumstances to the other. Once chapter, one of you can transfer a Condition or Tilt to the other (though the new subject must be a valid target for the Condition or Tilt - Stigmatic's can't be Burned after all, for example). Henceforth, the Condition or Tilt is treated as if the new target was the one to gain it.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Share Pain</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Shared Burden<br /> <b>Effect</b>: Your bond now allows for individual wounds and general health to be transfered to your other half. Once per scene, you may make a Intelligence + Medicine roll, and can transfer up to successes in Bashing damage (or trading in two successes for one Lethal damage transfered). You can now also transfer Conditions or Tilts from Shared Burden up to once per day.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Bounce Signal</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite</b>: Sympathetic Stigmatic<br /> <b>Effect</b>: You have figured out how to bounce the signal of your Aetheric Resonance off of your Sympathetic Stigmatic. Whenever you perform action that would trigger Aetheric detection, you can opt to have the source appear to be the Stigmatic.<br /> <b>Drawback</b>: Having your Stigmatic appear to be the source of Aether is a good way to draw Demonic and Cryptid attention.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Suppress Signal</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite</b>: Sympathetic Demon, Demon with Bounce Signal<br /> <b>Effect</b>: You can now fully contain your Demon's Aetheric signal inside yourself, preventing any leakage, for 1 full day by spending a point of Willpower. The Demon can exist in Demonic Form during this time without Compromise, and this effect suppresses the Burned Condition for its duration. Other Compromise checks due to Aetheric Resonance can be canceled by spending additional Willpower points.<br /> <b>Drawback</b>: Whenever you are actively suppressing your Demon's Aetheric signal inside yourself, your Willpower is treat as one lower, and you have a -1 penalty to all skill rolls.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Sympathetic Synergy</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite</b>: Sympathetic Stigmatic or Sympathetic Demon<br /> <b>Effect</b>: When you are near your sympathetic other half, you intuitive understanding of each other bolsters your teamwork. Whenever you are the primary actor in a teamwork roll, your sympathetic other half adds +2 instead of the normal +1 to your roll. If you are the secondary actor to their primary roll, you may forgo adding dice and instead grant them 9-again (or 8-again, if they already have 9-again) on their roll.<br /> [Creator's Notes: This is pretty much a more limited version of the 1ed Fairest Playmate Kith bonus.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-10-2016, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T05:35:00-08:00","id":805166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=805154#post805154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now some stuff for Sympathetic Stigmatics and Demons:</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again, I am impressed by all the Merits you're posting here in this thread. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And I eagerly await the rest. These look like the sort of Merits you could expect on a Stigmatic that the Demon might consider as a True Friend.<br /> <br /> <sub>P.S: You planning on fixing the layout for them? Bold sections and all that?</sub>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T07:46:08-08:00","id":805235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=805166#post805166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><sub>P.S: You planning on fixing the layout for them? Bold sections and all that?</sub></div> </div> </div> </div>Updated. <hr /><br /> Placeholders and notes for some other ideas.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Soul Crafter</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Soul Collector, the Hellhounds Exploit.<br /> <b>Effect</b>: You can now use the Hellhounds Exploit upon a soul in your possession. First create a ghost of a Rank equal to half your Primum, round up, then apply the Cryptid template (with an Rank equal to the ghost's) as per the Hellhounds Exploit. The resultant creation must possess the Twilight Form Adaptation.<br /> [Notes: Spec Aether Dependency as a Cryptid adaptation the Hellhounds get for free, since it is more of a penalty?]<br /> <br /> <b><u>Soul Burner</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Soul Collector<br /> <b>Effect: </b>You can 'burn' souls for power, converting their essence into Aether that can be used to fuel your own powers. By sacrificing one dot of a given soul's Integrity, you can make a Resolve + Composure roll to harvest the Aether produced. Each success grants you a point of Aether.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> The amount of Aether discharged by this act can serve as a beacon to the God-Machine. Every time this Merit is invoked, you must make a compromise roll at a penalty equal to the successes in the harvest roll. Furthermore, you take the Demonic Disconnect Condition, and can only resolve it by failing a Social roll with a human being.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Aetheric Insulation</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Soul Collector<br /> <b>Effect</b>: You can route Aetheric Resonance through a soul you own. Whenever you would trigger a Compromise roll through Demonic power (such as for Demonic Form transformations, Exploits, etc., but not for acting out of Cover, or being investigated), you may make the Compromise roll using the soul's Integrity instead. Upon failure, decrease the soul's Integrity instead.<br /> <br /> [Notes: Add the effects of Soul Burner and Aetheric Insulation as Pact options? &quot;Hey, I'll offer you power and riches, if you maybe let me use your soul/sanity as fuel from time to time. Don't worry, it's recoverable.&quot;]<br /> <br /> <u><b>Cannibalization</b></u><b> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Effect:</b> Whenever you deal fatal damage to another Demon, or come upon the corpse of a deceased Unchained within a number of minutes equal to your Primum, you may take one of that Demon's Form powers for your own, adding it to your total. If you already have the maximum number of Form powers allowed, you can keep this extra one for 1 lunar month (at least long enough to make it into a Form Gadget), after which it degrades to nothing.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Similar to the concept of cellular memory, you experience the residual emotions tied to the deceased's final moments. Upon acquiring the Form power, roll Resolve + Composure at a penalty equal to half the deceased's Primum (rounded up). On a failure, you gain the Demonic Rage Condition, which can only be resolved when he kills someone.<br /> <b>Note</b>: If you are using Angelic Form Abilities (as detailed <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities\">here</a>), then this Merit also applies to those abilities, though a Demon can only steal the &quot;Fallen&quot; version of them from Angels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-07-2016, 07:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T08:13:03-08:00","id":805251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=805235#post805235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Updated. <hr /><br /> Placeholders and notes for some other ideas.<br /> <br /> Soul Crafter \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022?<br /> Prerequisites: Soul Collector, the Hellhounds Exploit.<br /> Effect: You can now use the Hellhounds Exploit upon a soul in your possession. First make a ghost of a Rank equal to half your Primum, round up, then apply the Cryptid template (with an Rank equal to the ghost base's). The resultant creation is a ghost-Cryptid loyal to you and dependent upon Aether.<br /> [Spec Aether Dependency as a Cryptid adaptation the Hellhounds get for free, since it is more of a penalty?]<br /> <br /> Soul Burner \u2022\u2022\u2022?<br /> Prerequisites: Soul Collector<br /> Effect: [Track a soul's Integrity here, or make a note of it in Soul Collector?] You can &quot;burn&quot; souls for Aether. Decrease the soul's Integrity by 1, and make an Aether Harvesting roll.<br /> <br /> Aetheric Insulation \u2022\u2022\u2022?<br /> Prerequisites: Soul Collector<br /> Effect: You can route Aetheric Resonance through a soul you own. Whenever you would trigger a Compromise roll through Demonic power (such as for Demonic Form transformations, Exploits, etc., but not for acting out of Cover, or being investigated), you may make the Compromise roll using the soul's Integrity instead. Upon failure, decrease the soul's Integrity instead.<br /> [Add the effects of these two merits as Pact options?]<br /> <br /> Cannibalization \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022?<br /> Effect: Whenever you deal fatal damage to another Demon, or reach a recently dead Unchained within your Primum turns, you may take one of that Demon's Form powers for your own, adding it to your total. If you already have the maximum number of Form powers allowed, you can keep this extra one for 1 lunar month (at least long enough to make it into a Form Gadget), after which it degrades to nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha I don't even know how you keep on thinking these merits up. Please keep them coming. So great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T08:18:50-08:00","id":805256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=805235#post805235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soul Crafter \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022?<br /> Prerequisites: Soul Collector, the Hellhounds Exploit.<br /> Effect: You can now use the Hellhounds Exploit upon a soul in your possession. First make a ghost of a Rank equal to half your Primum, round up, then apply the Cryptid template (with an Rank equal to the ghost base's). The resultant creation is a ghost-Cryptid loyal to you and dependent upon Aether.<br /> <br /> [Spec Aether Dependency as a Cryptid adaptation the Hellhounds get for free, since it is more of a penalty?]</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd make it a three-dot Merit. Could you elaborate, though, on the last point? I don't quite follow on Aether Dependency with regards to the Exploit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=805235#post805235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soul Burner \u2022\u2022\u2022?<br /> Prerequisites: Soul Collector<br /> Effect: [Track a soul's Integrity here, or make a note of it in Soul Collector?] You can &quot;burn&quot; souls for Aether. Decrease the soul's Integrity by 1, and make an Aether Harvesting roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep it at three dots. And perhaps rephrase the description as this...<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Effect: </b>You can 'burn' souls for power, converting their essence into Aether that can be used to fuel your own powers. By sacrificing one dot of a given soul's Integrity, you can make a Resolve + Composure roll to harvest the Aether produced. Each success grants you a point of Aether.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback:</b> The amount of Aether discharged by this act can serve as a beacon to the God-Machine. Every time this Merit is invoked, you must make a compromise roll at a penalty equal to the successes in the harvest roll. Furthermore, you take the Demonic Disconnect Condition, and can only resolve it by failing a Social roll with a human being.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=805235#post805235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aetheric Insulation \u2022\u2022\u2022?<br /> Prerequisites: Soul Collector<br /> Effect: You can route Aetheric Resonance through a soul you own. Whenever you would trigger a Compromise roll through Demonic power (such as for Demonic Form transformations, Exploits, etc., but not for acting out of Cover, or being investigated), you may make the Compromise roll using the soul's Integrity instead. Upon failure, decrease the soul's Integrity instead.<br /> <br /> [Add the effects of these two merits as Pact options?]</div> </div> </div> </div>Three-dot Merit. And I'm not entirely sure I'd make it (and Soul Burner) as a Pact option. Either way, Aetheric Insulation works very well with Soul Burner if you choose to weave in my suggested drawback.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=805235#post805235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cannibalization \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022?</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely a five-dot Merit, especially given the possible applications for it. Also, I have a few suggestions...<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> Whenever you deal fatal damage to another Demon, or come upon the corpse of a deceased Unchained within a number of minutes equal to your Primum, you may take one of that Demon's Form powers for your own, adding it to your total. If you already have the maximum number of Form powers allowed, you can keep this extra one for 1 lunar month (at least long enough to make it into a Form Gadget), after which it degrades to nothing.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Similar to the concept of cellular memory, you experience the residual emotions tied to the deceased's final moments. Upon acquiring the Form power, roll Resolve + Composure at a penalty equal to half the deceased's Primum (rounded up). On a failure, you gain the Demonic Rage Condition, which can only be resolved when he kills someone.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> Alternatively, I could consider prompting a Glitch roll, with a bonus equal to half the deceased's Primum (rounded up). And in the event that you already are at the maximum number of Form powers, maybe the extra Modification/Technology/Propulsion/Process lasts for a number of days/weeks equal to your Primum? This could reflect your Aetheric Soul having a weak connection due to being at full processing power, and it's only a matter of time before said connection 'burns out'.<br /> <br /> <sub>And do make the descriptors bold with this batch, too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></sub>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-10-2016, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T08:19:54-08:00","id":805257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=805251#post805251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Haha I don't even know how you keep on thinking these merits up. Please keep them coming. So great.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, the Soul-based ones were:<br /> <br /> &quot;Huh, Raise Dead and Form Gadget burnout require Souls, but Demon's don't have any actual way to provide them.&quot;<br /> <br /> &lt;Thinks up Soul Collector&gt;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, those are niche situations. What <i>else</i> can a Demon get up to, once it has Souls? Aether supply for a rainy day? You know, non-Animal Hellhounds would be cool.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T08:28:47-08:00","id":805264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=805257#post805257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What <i>else</i> can a Demon get up to, once it has Souls? Aether supply for a rainy day? You know, non-Animal Hellhounds would be cool.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This just made me think of the Larvae from Dungeons and Dragons, seeing as they <i>are</i> mortal souls that end up in the Abyss and eventually get twisted into demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T08:39:13-08:00","id":805273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=805256#post805256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd make it a three-dot Merit. Could you elaborate, though, on the last point? I don't quite follow on Aether Dependency with regards to the Exploit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cryptids created with Hellhounds require 1 Aether a day per size, or they die. Frankly, I find that ridiculously high, and house rule otherwise, but there it is. I was thinking of writing up a Aether Dependency Adaptation/Quality, once I've settled on it's final form. Makes a quick short hand, and is useful for giving certain Cryptids urgency.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=805256#post805256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Drawback:</b> The amount of Aether discharged by this act can serve as a beacon to the God-Machine. Every time this Merit is invoked, you must make a compromise roll at a penalty equal to the successes in the harvest roll. Furthermore, you take the Demonic Disconnect Condition, and can only resolve it by failing a Social roll with a human being.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems kinda excessive, after all the trouble the Demon already had to go to to get the Soul. Included anyways, though. Aether is supposed to be not easily acquired.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=805256#post805256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Three-dot Merit. And I'm not entirely sure I'd make it (and Soul Burner) as a Pact option. Either way, Aetheric Insulation works very well with Soul Burner if you choose to weave in my suggested drawback.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea was for other Faustian options for Pacts. Currently the cost to mortals is &quot;social context&quot; and &quot;oblivion&quot;. Maybe &quot;loyal cultist&quot;? This might offer to story elements of someone knowing there is a Demonic sword hanging over their head, waiting for it to fall, yet still is short of the threat of total annihilation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=805256#post805256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><sub>And do make the descriptors bold with this batch, too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></sub></div> </div> </div> </div>Done.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T08:49:34-08:00","id":805277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=805273#post805273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems kinda excessive, after all the trouble the Demon already had to go to to get the Soul. Included anyways, though. Aether is supposed to be not easily acquired.</div> </div> </div> </div>And admittedly, 'flaying' a soul for power isn't exactly subtle from a metaphysical standpoint. Plus, even if they aren't human, Demons relate to Humanity. And when one is essentially using a mortal soul as a 'living battery charger', it is bound to cause him to dissociate himself from the 'cattle'.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=805273#post805273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea was for other Faustian options for Pacts. Currently the cost to mortals is &quot;social context&quot; and &quot;oblivion&quot;. Maybe &quot;loyal cultist&quot;? This might offer to story elements of someone knowing there is a Demonic sword hanging over their head, waiting for it to fall, yet still is short of the threat of total annihilation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of like the Pishogue Sanction of Changeling pledges. Except, in this case, it's &quot;death by 1,000 cuts&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T11:21:50-08:00","id":805363,"title":"","content":"Thoughts on this addition to the Summon Demon merit?<br /> <br /> <b>Note</b>: If you already possess Sleeve Integrator, whenever you summon your Demon to you, you may opt to activate Sleeve Integrator at the same time. In this case, instead of appearing nearby, the Demon takes your identity as Cover seamlessly, as per Sleeve Integrator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T11:26:25-08:00","id":805367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=805363#post805363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thoughts on this addition to the Summon Demon merit?<br /> <br /> <b>Note</b>: If you already possess Sleeve Integrator, whenever you summon your Demon to you, you may opt to activate Sleeve Integrator at the same time. In this case, instead of appearing nearby, the Demon takes your identity as Cover seamlessly, as per Sleeve Integrator.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I definitely like this addition. It certainly puts an interesting twist to the term &quot;out of body experience&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T12:00:46-08:00","id":805387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=805367#post805367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I definitely like this addition. It certainly puts an interesting twist to the term &quot;out of body experience&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Updated.<br /> <br /> Yeah, it's great for the &quot;You aren't talking to John anymore&quot; scene where said Stigmatic is cornered, and then suddenly their Demon ally is there.<br /> <hr /><br /> Hmm. Anyone know if Unchained can offer Supernatural Merits as Benefits in a Pact?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-10-2016, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T12:18:45-08:00","id":805394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=805387#post805387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. Anyone know if Unchained can offer Supernatural Merits as Benefits in a Pact?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, there isn't any rule saying you <i>can't</i>...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T04:35:42-08:00","id":806902,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8180\" data-vbnamecard=\"8180\">Deionscribe</a> : Do you want me to edit my first post to compile all of the merits I wrote there? Makes it easier if the content is on the first page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T04:39:22-08:00","id":806906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=806902#post806902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8180\" data-vbnamecard=\"8180\">Deionscribe</a> : Do you want me to edit my first post to compile all of the merits I wrote there? Makes it easier if the content is on the first page.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I might make a google doc for everything and keep the forum as a place for future additions.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1TeBwffI5hBVlbE_B_KhTPjU3cnG0L7oR_6RbGq8YX94/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Here's the G-Doc.</a>.<br /> <br /> I might consider redoing how I sorted them out. But for now, they're arranged in alphabetical order and ascending dot rating. I also flagged the Gadgeteer Merit for clarification, because I wasn't sure what you meant with the Drawback besides mention of a possible Aether expenditure.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-12-2016, 09:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T09:10:34-08:00","id":807063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=806906#post806906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, I might make a google doc for everything and keep the forum as a place for future additions.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1TeBwffI5hBVlbE_B_KhTPjU3cnG0L7oR_6RbGq8YX94/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Here's the G-Doc.</a>.<br /> <br /> I might consider redoing how I sorted them out. But for now, they're arranged in alphabetical order and ascending dot rating. I also flagged the Gadgeteer Merit for clarification, because I wasn't sure what you meant with the Drawback besides mention of a possible Aether expenditure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Maybe group some of them by Prerequisite? It's kind of confusing to see a pre-req listed before knowing what it is. But it's not like that doesn't happen in the actual books too...<br /> <br /> I'm got a few ideas for some revisions and clarifications. Edit the source post and notify you to update the doc, PM you, or some other method?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T09:27:32-08:00","id":807078,"title":"","content":"A PM works. Looking forward to it.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T12:11:12-08:00","id":807200,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Idea for a bridge between Cohabitation and Quantum Synthesis:<br /> <br /> [I'd use Dual Processes if it wasn't already taken by Terrible Form \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022. Multi-threading, maybe? Probably not Cheerleader] \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Prerequisite</b>: Cohabitation<br /> <b>Effect</b>: You can now do more than merely advise the Demon using your identity as a Cover - now you can assist with tasks as well. Whenever the Demon is performing a mental action (such as rolls involving Mental Attributes, and some Social rolls, if advice alone would help), you may attempt to aid them as per the Teamwork rules.<br /> [Drawback: If necessary, maybe it inflicts some tiring condition after the merge ends? Duration or severity dependent upon the number of assists? Instead apply this drawback toward the far more effective Quantum Synthesis?]<br /> <br /> This also has the amusing mental image of the <i>Stigmatic</i> being the &quot;shoulder angel/devil&quot; giving advice. <hr /><br /> Hmm. Should some of the Demon specific terminology be broadened? Because I think some of the merits/abilities/power might also work with Angels, unless I am mistaken. Angels use Covers too...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-12-2016, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T14:31:33-08:00","id":807304,"title":"","content":"Since the Storyteller's Guide came out, I've been of the opinion that an Angel could take advantage of Sleeve Integrator (and therefore a lot of these Merits here) because I kind of like the idea of Stigmatics being caught, willingly or otherwise, between two sides of a long, drawn-out Cold War between the Unchained and the God-Machine. Like it or not, it would take one hell of a Stigmatic to assure their independence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T14:54:57-08:00","id":807324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=807304#post807304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the Storyteller's Guide came out, I've been of the opinion that an Angel could take advantage of Sleeve Integrator (and therefore a lot of these Merits here) because I kind of like the idea of Stigmatics being caught, willingly or otherwise, between two sides of a long, drawn-out Cold War between the Unchained and the God-Machine. Like it or not, it would take one hell of a Stigmatic to assure their independence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Medium's been around for a while, mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T15:47:34-08:00","id":807366,"title":"","content":"I keep forgetting that Medium applied to all Ephemeral Beings. I keep thinking of it as a Ghost and Spirit only thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T19:11:31-08:00","id":807511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=807366#post807366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep forgetting that Medium applied to all Ephemeral Beings. I keep thinking of it as a Ghost and Spirit only thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yep. Lists Infrastructure as one of the Conditions it can cause. Though I might add some wording to allow some of the Sleeve Integrator line to work with standard &quot;possession&quot;. Maybe an extra Merit, to focus your new &quot;skills&quot; on a more common &quot;problem&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T23:34:27-08:00","id":813945,"title":"","content":"Hmm. More Sympathetic X merit ideas.<br /> <br /> What about one that lets either of you use the other's Willpower (enabling you to go over the 1/turn cap, and thus truly ramp up rolls/resistance when needed)?<br /> Allow each to fulfill the other's Aspirations and get XP/Beats for it? Bonuses when acting towards the others Aspirations?<br /> Allow the Stigmatic to use the Demon's Interlocks?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T05:01:35-08:00","id":814050,"title":"","content":"The one for Willpower's a good concept. As is the ability for a Stigmatic to use his Demon's Interlocks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T18:40:49-08:00","id":830669,"title":"","content":"You know, I've been thinking that certain Demons might not be fully satisfied with the &quot;shape-shifting&quot; allowed by Covers, the Ephemeral Cover Exploit and Show Of Power. A few might even think it would be cool to live up to the fame of certain mythological fiends that had much more free-form transformations. At first, I considered a Lambda Gadget, but that seemed too external. My current idea is a pair of Merits that expands upon Hellhound and Ephemeral Cover. The name might need some improvement. I imagine that Unchained!Nyarlathotep would have many field days with these Merits, especially when combined with the Cipher that Eremite wrote for him. Feedback is super appreciated.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Genetic Morphing Field</b></u> (\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Hellhound Exploit, Stamina 3, Resolve 3, Science or Occult 3<br /> <br /> <b>Effects: </b>The Demon can use the Hellhound Exploit on himself, with a few differences. Spend 1 Aether + 1 willpower point and roll the normal dice pool as an instant action (the willpower point cancels the compromise roll as usual for Exploits). With a Success, he can transform into any animal of up to Size 10 for the scene. An Exceptional Success increases the duration to [Primum] days. During this, he can shift between different animal forms as an instant action with 1 Aether, and back to the Cover he last used reflexively without spending Aether. Transforming into an animal that is grossly inaccurate for the region requires a compromise roll.<br /> <br /> The Demon does not get [Primum + Successes] as extra dots to his stats. He uses the animal's Physical Attributes, Size and Speed Factor, but keeps his other stats. Additionally, he can assume a partial or complete Demonic Form, with the same benefits and drawbacks as usual. He retains the general appearance of the animal if he does this. He may use Spoofing to register as a mundane animal, with the rating of the Cover he last used. He may communicate as the animal would with a successful Wits + Animal Ken roll. He lacks the necessary anatomy to speak with a human voice, but may use Embeds, Exploits, Demon Form and Gadgets to communicate in other ways.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Corpus Reconfiguration</b></u> (\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>An Ephemeral Cover, Occult 3, Subterfuge 3<br /> <br /> <b>Effects:</b> The Demon can make the most out of a ghost or spirit Cover by changing its appearance to a different sub-type. Spend 1 Aether and roll Finesse + Primum as an instant action. On a Success, the Demon can make cosmetic changes that are substantial enough to be mistaken for another, which last for the scene. With an Exceptional Success, the change can last up to [Primum] days. The ghost of a murder victim will still carry signs of how it was killed, but the method may change from a gunshot to drowning. A spirit of lust can embody another Vice, but can't turn into a car spirit. In either case, facial features and other identifying markers will also change. Spoofing is still available to register as the appropriate ephemeral.<br /> <br /> With the four dot version, more dramatic changes can be made. By spending 3 Aether + 1 willpower point as an instant action, the Demon gains a pool of dots equal to his [Primum x 2] to distribute among the three simplified Attributes and Size. Use the <b><i>increased</i></b> Finesse + Primum as the dice pool. Each Attribute has a maximum of 15 dots, and their sum determines the Rank of the Cover. Size can be up to 10. The duration is the same as the ones listed for the Success and Exceptional Success of the two dot version of this Merit. The Demon may steal Essence points from ephemerals of the same type and convert them to Aether with a Power + Brawl or Weaponry roll, but halved round up. If the Demon exceeds the target's Rank by 2 or more, he counts as a Bane. The ephemeral Cover's natural weaponry have a lethal Damage Bonus equal to the Demon's Primum, but every dot above 5 becomes one point of Armor Piercing. Many Demons with the four dot version of this Merit also learn Rip The Gates and Show Of Power to enter the Underworld and the Shadow to further refine their mimicry. At the ST's discretion, a Demon with the four dot version may imitate entities such as Geister and Hosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 02-15-2016, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T01:50:58-08:00","id":830908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=830669#post830669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I've been thinking that certain Demons might not be fully satisfied with the &quot;shape-shifting&quot; allowed by Covers, the Ephemeral Cover Exploit and Show Of Power. A few might even think it would be cool to live up to the fame of certain mythological fiends that had much more free-form transformations. At first, I considered a Lambda Gadget, but that seemed too external. My current idea is a pair of Merits that expands upon Hellhound and Ephemeral Cover. The name might need some improvement. I imagine that Unchained!Nyarlathotep would have many field days with these Merits, especially when combined with the Cipher that Eremite wrote for him. Feedback is super appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are definitely interesting, though I do see a few grammar errors here and there. But that's easily rectified. And I think the names are also nice.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T10:56:01-08:00","id":837665,"title":"","content":"Question: is it possible to have Spirit Minions? Similar to Staff, or CtL Hobkin merit? If you use the Hellhounds exploit on a Spirit, could you treat it like a Familiar?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T11:07:42-08:00","id":837671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=837665#post837665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: is it possible to have Spirit Minions? Similar to Staff, or CtL Hobkin merit? If you use the Hellhounds exploit on a Spirit, could you treat it like a Familiar?</div> </div> </div> </div>As it currently reads, <u>Hellhounds</u> needs to target animals, so spirits aren't allowed.<br /> <br /> ...Having said that, please see Soul Crafter <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=805235#post805235\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> It might be nice to have a Familiar equivalent, but the nearest option are Rank 1 Angels/Imperatives which presents... problems. Maybe a Cryptid?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 02-26-2016, 02:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T11:12:27-08:00","id":837677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=830669#post830669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I've been thinking that certain Demons might not be fully satisfied with the &quot;shape-shifting&quot; allowed by Covers, the Ephemeral Cover Exploit and Show Of Power. A few might even think it would be cool to live up to the fame of certain mythological fiends that had much more free-form transformations. At first, I considered a Lambda Gadget, but that seemed too external. My current idea is a pair of Merits that expands upon Hellhound and Ephemeral Cover. The name might need some improvement. I imagine that Unchained!Nyarlathotep would have many field days with these Merits, especially when combined with the Cipher that Eremite wrote for him. Feedback is super appreciated.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Genetic Morphing Field</b></u> (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I'd be in favor of an Embed and Exploit combo that does what you have here. Embed for the &quot;appearance only&quot; change, like <u>Quick Change</u>, but with facial/body features. And an Exploit for the whole &quot;turn into an animal/plant/statue/whatever&quot; effect, usable on others (as well as oneself) for that whole &quot;frog curse&quot; option.<br /> <br /> Maybe a Homebrew Embeds and Exploits thread needs to get created/reopened...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T11:41:09-08:00","id":837691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=837677#post837677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, I'd be in favor of an Embed and Exploit combo that does what you have here. Embed for the &amp;quot;appearance only&amp;quot; change, like <u>Quick Change</u>, but with facial/body features. And an Exploit for the whole &amp;quot;turn into an animal/plant/statue/whatever&amp;quot; effect, usable on others (as well as oneself) for that whole &amp;quot;frog curse&amp;quot; option.<br /> <br /> Maybe a Homebrew Embeds and Exploits thread needs to get created/reopened...</div> </div> </div> </div>That can be arranged.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I can get to it once I got time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T11:43:53-08:00","id":837693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=837691#post837691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That can be arranged.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I can get to it once I got time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good. I've got at least 14 bouncing around in my notes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T12:34:16-08:00","id":837713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=837693#post837693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good. I've got at least 14 bouncing around in my notes.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits\">Here you go.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T10:21:25-08:00","id":839282,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Ephemeral Adaptation</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Sleeve Integrator, Medium, Occult \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Effect: </b>You figured out how to leverage your talents with serving as a Demon's Cover to influencing your interactions with ephemeral entities. You can now treat other ephemeral beings as if they were Demons for the purpose of the Sleeve Integrator merit, and other merits derived from it. Instead of the ephemeral using you as a Cover, however, you can offer it the ability to Possess you as if it had the Possession Manifestation (even if it would not qualify for it). Instead of acquiring Embeds, you may gain any combination of Influence dots or Numina (up to your dots in Sleeve Integrator) the being possesses, paying for them with Willpower instead.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Unified Will</u> \u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Inherent Connection<br /> <b>Effect</b>: You have achieved such synchronization with your other half that your wills can bolster each other beyond normal limits. You can now spend Willpower from your sympathetic other half's pool in addition to your own (granting up to +6 to a roll, +4 for resistance, powering 2 abilities that cost Willpower, etc.)<br /> <b>Drawback</b>: Willpower expenditure is Willpower expenditure, even if it isn't used for yourself. Tapping the other party's Willpower also counts as their per-turn Willpower limit (usually 1).<br /> <b>Note</b>: This is a companion Merit to the Unified Will possessed by the other half of Sympathetic Stigmatic/Demon.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Interlocking Sympathy</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Inherent Connection, Stigmatic only<br /> <b>Effect</b>: Your close bond with your Demon also allows you to access the same hacks and tricks that are close to their identity. You can now employ your sympathetic Demon's Interlocks as if you possessed them.<br /> <b>Notes</b>: You may spend a point of Willpower to pay for Aether costs (if any) that the Interlock possesses. If the Interlock calls for a Compromise check, you make an Integrity check at the same bonus or penalty.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Soul Emulation</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Soul Collector<br /> <b>Effect</b>: You can now make use of a soul just like the beings that normally possess them, such as for the purposes of Abjuration, Warding, etc. Use the soul's Integrity for such rolls when called for. Dramatic failures on such rolls reduce the stored soul's Integrity by 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-16-2017, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T10:09:02-08:00","id":841372,"title":"","content":"Hmmm. Would &quot;high-level&quot; Merits make sense? You know, those that require Primum 6+ for &quot;End Game&quot; play (like Equinox Road).<br /> <br /> Would one that let's you take Supernatural Merits for your Cover(s) fit?<br /> What about one that let's you take on an &quot;institution&quot; as a Cover (like Demon House on steroids)?<br /> What about creating mini-Occult Matrixes, for more free-form effects, or limited Infrastructure?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T14:21:39-08:00","id":842154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=841372#post841372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm. Would &amp;quot;high-level&amp;quot; Merits make sense? You know, those that require Primum 6+ for &amp;quot;End Game&amp;quot; play (like Equinox Road).<br /> <br /> Would one that let's you take Supernatural Merits for your Cover(s) fit?<br /> What about one that let's you take on an &amp;quot;institution&amp;quot; as a Cover (like Demon House on steroids)?<br /> What about creating mini-Occult Matrixes, for more free-form effects, or limited Infrastructure?</div> </div> </div> </div>I could definitely see those as options. You could also make the final secret of the cipher a merit that could be representative of end level play. Or maybe they could be tied to high level agencies and what they specialize in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T20:21:54-07:00","id":847499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=841372#post841372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm. Would &quot;high-level&quot; Merits make sense? You know, those that require Primum 6+ for &quot;End Game&quot; play (like Equinox Road).<br /> <br /> Would one that let's you take Supernatural Merits for your Cover(s) fit?<br /> What about one that let's you take on an &quot;institution&quot; as a Cover (like Demon House on steroids)?<br /> What about creating mini-Occult Matrixes, for more free-form effects, or limited Infrastructure?</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd like to see that. It should be noted that the epic Changelings described in Equinox Road are more mythological and poetic. Epic Demons are more like the stuff of the wildest conspiracy theories: godlike aliens tampering with the development of humanity for inscrutable purposes and such. In that sense, they are ironically quite Angel-like.<br /> <br /> Besides Merits, Epic Demons could have unique Demonic Form advantages based on their personalities and goals, similar to Ciphers.<br /> <br /> I'd like to share an Epic Demon Merit. The name is a play on the term &quot;God Mode&quot;, which means a cheat code that makes you invincible in a video game. The drawback could inflict a new Persistent Condition that halves the dice pools of all supernatural powers round down, if you prefer that. I don't know what could Resolve such a Condition, though.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Lucifer Mode</u> (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Primum 5 or 6 (whichever you prefer), Resolve 3, Composure 3, Occult 3</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Effect</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: When Going Loud, your Demon can choose three Attributes to increase to 10, along with their Primum. Derived traits are changed accordingly. Additionally, the cap of 10 on your Willpower dots is removed, with </span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">all willpower points being restored.</span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Finally, all rolls to Contest supernatural powers or perform a Clash Of Wills receive 8 Again. All of this stacks with other Merits, Gadgets, Embeds, Exploits, Interlocks and Demonic Form advantages.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Drawback</b>: Roll half of your Demon's normal Resolve + Composure, rounded down and with no willpower expenditure allowed. On a Failure, they must roll for a permanent Glitch using their maxed out Primum, which applies to the next Cover they use.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-14-2016, 11:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T20:38:29-07:00","id":847508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=847499#post847499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'd like to see Merits like that. It should be noted that the epic Changelings described in Equinox Road are more mythological and poetic. Epic Demons are more like the stuff of the wildest conspiracy theories: godlike aliens tampering with the development of humanity for inscrutable purposes and such. In that sense, they are ironically quite Angel-like.<br /> <br /> Besides Merits, Epic Demons could have unique Demonic Form advantages based on their personalities and goals, similar to Ciphers.<br /> <br /> I'd like to share an Epic Demon Merit. The name is a play on the term &amp;quot;God Mode&amp;quot;, which means a cheat code that makes you invincible in a video game. The drawback could inflict a new Persistent Condition that halves the dice pools of all supernatural powers round down, if you prefer that. I don't know what could Resolve such a Condition, though.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Lucifer Mode</u> (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Primum 5 or 6 (whichever you prefer), Resolve 3, Composure 3, Occult 3</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Effect</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: When Going Loud, your Demon can choose three Attributes to increase to 10, along with their Primum. Derived traits are changed accordingly. Additionally, the cap of 10 on your Willpower dots is removed, with </span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">all willpower points being restored.</span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Finally, all rolls to Contest supernatural powers or perform a Clash Of Wills receive 8 Again. All of this stacks with other Merits, Gadgets, Embeds, Exploits, Interlocks and Demonic Form advantages.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Drawback</b>: Roll half of your Demon's normal Resolve + Composure, rounded down and with no willpower expenditure allowed. On a Failure, they must roll for a permanent Glitch using their maxed out Primum, which applies to the next Cover they use.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>O_O<br /> Give me a while to process my thoughts on this interesting Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T21:36:54-07:00","id":847531,"title":"","content":"Deionscribe, if you think Lucifer Mode is too much for one Merit, know that I thought of a more modular version: a Supernatural Style, with each Maneuver having a Primum prerequisite. Some Maneuvers would be accessible in full Demonic Form without Going Loud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T21:46:26-07:00","id":847535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=847531#post847531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deionscribe, if you think Lucifer Mode is too much for one Merit, know that I thought of a more modular version: a Supernatural Style, with each Maneuver having a Primum prerequisite. Some Maneuvers would be accessible in full Demonic Form without Going Loud.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm. Post it here when you have it done, and then I can compare the two versions.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T21:57:39-07:00","id":847541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=839282#post839282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Ephemeral Adaptation</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Sleeve Integrator, Medium, Occult \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Effect: </b>You figured out how to leverage your talents with serving as a Demon's Cover to influencing your interactions with ephemeral entities. You can now treat other ephemeral beings as if they were Demons for the purpose of the Sleeve Integrator merit, and other merits derived from it. Instead of the ephemeral using you as a Cover, however, you can offer it the ability to Possess you as if it had the Possession Manifestation (even if it would not qualify for it).<br /> <br /> <b><u>Unified Will</u> \u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Inherent Connection<br /> <b>Effect</b>: You have achieved such synchronization with your other half that your wills can bolster each other beyond normal limits. You can now spend Willpower from your sympathetic other half's pool in addition to your own (granting up to +6 to a roll, +4 for resistance, powering 2 abilities that cost Willpower, etc.)<br /> <b>Drawback</b>: Willpower expenditure is Willpower expenditure, even if it isn't used for yourself. Tapping the other party's Willpower also counts as their per-turn Willpower limit (usually 1).<br /> <b>Note</b>: This is a companion Merit to the Unified Will possessed by the other half of Sympathetic Stigmatic/Demon.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Interlocking Sympathy</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Inherent Connection, Stigmatic only<br /> <b>Effect</b>: Your close bond with your Demon also allows you to access the same hacks and tricks that are close to their identity. You can now employ your sympathetic Demon's Interlocks as if you possessed them.<br /> <b>Notes</b>: You may spend a point of Willpower to pay for Aether costs (if any) that the Interlock possesses. If the Interlock calls for a Compromise check, you make an Integrity check at the same bonus or penalty.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Soul Emulation</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Soul Collector<br /> <b>Effect</b>: You can now make use of a soul just like the beings that normally possess them, such as for the purposes of Abjuration, Warding, etc. Use the soul's Integrity for such rolls when called for. Dramatic failures on such rolls reduce the stored soul's Integrity by 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>Finally added these to the Doc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T22:04:18-07:00","id":847544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=847541#post847541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Finally added these to the Doc.</div> </div> </div> </div> By the way, any of you can add my stuff to that Doc. Don't forget to give my name. I'd just like to get feedback for each one and settle on a polished version before it is added.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T22:12:07-07:00","id":847547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=847544#post847544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> By the way, any of you can add my stuff to that Doc. Don't forget to give my name. I'd just like to get feedback for each one and settle on a polished version before it is added.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can post comments on the Doc, if you'd like. Already added your stuff in. Just browse around and post any revisions or additions you like.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> That said, added you to the list of contributors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T08:29:43-07:00","id":847701,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Supernatural Integration</u> \u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Primum 6, Show Of Power<br /> <b>Effect</b>: You can now hack &quot;extra-normal&quot; occult abilities into your Covers as easy as background details. You can spend Cover Experiences upon Supernatural Merits (with Dots no higher than your Dots in this Merit) for your Covers, as if you were a mortal.<br /> <b>Drawback</b>: Such Merits are tied exclusively to the Cover they are purchased for, and so the Demon must be in that Cover to use them. Such Merits are not protected by the Sanctity of Merits rule should the Demon lose that Cover.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Institutional Cover</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Primum 6, Demon House<br /> <b>Effect</b>: You can now craft a Patchwork Cover for an <i>Institution</i>, directing and influencing its various component members. You are considered to have the Demon House Exploit in effect for all of the Institution's resources (such as office space, employees during work hours, ritual chambers, etc.), with the exception that your Institutional Cover never degrades for being in it for days (though your other Covers might from neglect). You can make Pacts with the executive officers and leadership positions of other organizations to acquire Cover elements as if making a Pact with a human. When in your Institutional Cover, you are treated as a Organization/Conspiracy, with a Power, Finesse, and Resistance of the highest of your rating in those categories (capped by Standing), and an effective Standing equal to the lower of your Cover rating or Primum.<br /> <b>Drawback</b>: You need to anchor your presences around each resource with something material - a Lynch Pin, in other words. Additionally, Institutions have more &quot;surface area&quot; than individuals, and are more prone to investigation.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: Drifting around in my head ever since reading about &quot;Institutional Demons&quot; in Mortal Remains and thinking &quot;wait, that doesn't describe Unchained at all. ...but could it?&quot;. Also inspired by frequent references to bureaucracies being self-preserving organisms in the Laundry books.]<br /> <br /> <b><u>Occult Experimentation</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Primum 8, 4 Embeds in each Category, 4 Exploits<br /> <b>Effect</b>: You now know (or can guess) enough about the occult physics that power Occult Matrices than you can now attempt basic, jury-rigged ones yourself. You can now access the Occult Matrix sub-system.<br /> <b>Note</b>: This isn't remotely close to done. Basic suggestions - Copy the general ritual systems off of something like Blood Sorcery, add in some research rolls to even cobble a potential Matrix together, then have a number of ingredients and/or extended actions to actually fire it off, then dial the effects up to 11 for all the trouble. Each such working is single use only, though some research discounts might be appropriate for merely changing a few variables.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: Basically, more free-form abilities. Being able to justify your own Plot Device effect is nice, too. High-end effects might even be being able to &quot;create&quot; your own auto-Exile Rank 1-2 Angels, if you want to get crazy.]<br /> <br /> <b><u>Shield of Deception</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Primum 6<br /> <b>Effect</b>: Whenever you are rolling to resist or contest an ability that includes Supernatural Tolerance in your roll, from a source that does not know for certain you are a Demon, your can add Cover <i>and</i> Primum to your roll, instead of only one of them.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Cryptologist</b></u> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Primum 6, Hellhounds, Show Of Power<br /> <b>Effect</b>: Long experimentation and study has given the Demon new insights into Cryptid forms and abilities. [They can create Cryptids with the Hellhounds Exploit that do not require Aether for survival? They can give Cryptids one Adaptation that replicates the powers or abilities of another being (such as Demonic Exploits, or anything that Show Of Power could replicate)? They can use Hellhounds on non-animal targets, like other people or pre-existing Cryptids?]<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: I don't really know where I want to go with this. Improving Cryptid creation would be easier if there were more rules actually regarding it.]<br /> <br /> <b><u>Evolved Form</u> \u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Style</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Primum 5+dots<br /> <b>Effect</b>: You have figured out how to incorporate Lambda Form Gadgets into your Demonic Form as if they were a natural extension of yourself.<br /> <i>Mu Modification</i> (\u2022): You can graft a single Lambda containing a Modification Form ability to yourself, replacing or adding to your existing Modifications.<br /> <i>Tau Technology</i> (\u2022\u2022): You can graft a single Lambda containing a Technology Form ability to yourself, replacing or adding to your existing Technologies.<br /> <i>Phi Propulsion</i> (\u2022\u2022\u2022): You can graft a single Lambda containing a Propulsion Form ability to yourself, replacing or adding to your existing Propulsions.<br /> <i>Omega Process</i> (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): You can graft a single Lambda containing a Process Form ability to yourself, replacing or adding to your existing Processes.<br /> <i>Truly Unchained</i> (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): You are no longer limited to the number of Form Lambdas you can possess, though you can still only hold your normal limit of Form Abilities.<br /> <b>Note</b>: You must have the Form Lambda you wish to graft.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: You know you wanted to ever since you saw Form Gadgets, and that they could be re-grafted. Why <i>not</i> make a Form Gadget, make it into a Lambda, then re-add it back into your Form? Alternative names: Awesome Form, Deific Form, Apocalyptic Form]<br /> <br /> <b><u>Metaphysical Cover</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Primum 6, Play On Words<br /> <b>Effect</b>: The Demon can now <i>literally</i> &quot;hide behind&quot; their Cover, treating all ranged attacks against them for a turn as if they were behind cover with Durability equal to their current Cover rating, at the cost of one Willpower point.<br /> <b>Drawback</b>: Using your Cover as a metaphysical shield can have consequences. Any attack that breaches your &quot;cover&quot; forces you to roll for Compromise with a penalty equal to the damage (maximum of -5).<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: Should this even be a merit, or just something a cunning Demon can employ using Play On Words? Downplay the Drawback, or no because a high Cover Demon becomes practically bullet-proof?] <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Organizations</b></span><br /> <br /> Collections of individuals cannot be handled using simple NPCs Attributes or applying them in bulk - but they <i>can</i> still be modelled in the Chronicles of Darkness mechanics system. Treat them as an NPC with <b>Power</b> representing their direct ability to enforce their designs, <b>Finesse</b> representing their capacity for subtle influence and maneuvering, and <b>Resistance</b> representing their resilience to outside forces.<br /> Organizations have a <b>Virtue</b> and a <b>Vice</b>, like other characters, which represents the conflicting drives inherent their members and leadership.<br /> Organizations also have a set of <b>Principles</b>, which represent inner laws and guidelines members follow.<br /> And Organization also has Standing, which represents the general influence, power, and commitment of its members. Higher Standing allows for higher Attributes, additional Actions per Organization Turn, and contributes to dice pools the Organization makes.<br /> <br /> For additional details, please refer to Krewe Rules, in Geist: the Sin-Eaters (2nd Edition), or Conspiracy rules in Deviant: the Renegades. <hr /><br /> [Placeholder for Occult Matrix Sub-System(s)]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-06-2021, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T13:05:59-07:00","id":847810,"title":"","content":"Interesting ideas behind the Supernatural Integration Merit, Vent xD I can understand why the Supernatural Merits wouldn't fall under the Sanctity rules, but I have to ask. Do uses of them (or at least Dramatic Failures involving them) call for a Compromise roll?<br /> <br /> I can't say much yet on Institutional Cover or Occult Experimentation. But as high level/endgame Merits, they certainly look promising with what's already written down. Looking forward to you elaborating further on their respective systems.<br /> <br /> Shield of Deception packs quite a punch. I like it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> May I also suggest adding in a Merit that uses it as a prerequisite? One that allows you to spend Willpower to add your Primum as a bonus instead of (or in addition) to the regular benefits when resisting supernatural powers from someone aware of his nature? I even have a tentative name: Shield of the Unchained.<br /> <br /> Nice work on Cryptologist and Evolved Form <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> May need to look up the Cryptid creation rules and Lambda Gadgets forst before I can offer more input.<br /> <br /> For the last one, I'd say keep it as a Merit. It actually is pretty good as a concept. Though maybe downplay the drawback by adding that penalties stemming from damage in an attack roll can never exceed -5. And maybe the expenditure of a Wilpower point is required.<br /> <br /> As for a name, Metaphysical Cover was the only thing I could think up. Does that work? ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T13:44:00-07:00","id":847836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=847810#post847810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting ideas behind the Supernatural Integration Merit, Vent xD I can understand why the Supernatural Merits wouldn't fall under the Sanctity rules, but I have to ask. Do uses of them (or at least Dramatic Failures involving them) call for a Compromise roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe? At this point, you are still &quot;just another mortal - pay no attention&quot;, only you have some supernatural trick. Maybe you are confused for a Stigmatic? You are still within &quot;normal variation&quot;, if not more so - after all, Demons and other supernaturals <i>can't</i> acquire Supernatural Merits (baring exceptions, such as the above and that one Ordo Dracul Mystery/Coil).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=847810#post847810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't say much yet on Institutional Cover or Occult Experimentation. But as high level/endgame Merits, they certainly look promising with what's already written down. Looking forward to you elaborating further on their respective systems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. So am I. Though I'll likely need crowd-sourced help with those. It's these kind of open ended projects that get me mired into all the possibilities that nothing actually gets done.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=847810#post847810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shield of Deception packs quite a punch. I like it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> May I also suggest adding in a Merit that uses it as a prerequisite? One that allows you to spend Willpower to add your Primum as a bonus instead of (or in addition) to the regular benefits when resisting supernatural powers from someone aware of his nature? I even have a tentative name: Shield of the Unchained.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was inspired by the spoilers for Changeling 2ED (namely, adding Clarity to Resistance rolls against non-Fae powers). As for a follow-up power, sure. You can add that, if you want. Looks straight-forward. Though I added the &quot;doesn't know you are a Demon&quot; part to give it some weakness. Otherwise it's a pretty major power jump.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=847810#post847810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice work on Cryptologist and Evolved Form <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> May need to look up the Cryptid creation rules and Lambda Gadgets forst before I can offer more input.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cryptid creation rules are very bare bones. And Hellhounds lets you just whip them up. It's kinda frustrating. I actually house-ruled in restrictions on it to give it some structure. As it stands now, nothing prevents you from turning pidgeons in the park into Rank 5 Cryptid monstrosities that can tear through steel like tissue paper. Out of the box, at Primum 1.<br /> <br /> Lambda Gadgets are fun. Basically use two or three powers, then generate an effect based on the conceptual overlap.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=847810#post847810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the last one, I'd say keep it as a Merit. It actually is pretty good as a concept. Though maybe downplay the drawback by adding that penalties stemming from damage in an attack roll can never exceed -5. And maybe the expenditure of a Wilpower point is required.<br /> <br /> As for a name, Metaphysical Cover was the only thing I could think up. Does that work? ^^</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if it is costing Willpower, maybe I can remove the Auto-Compromise. I'll use the name, too, thanks.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T09:15:52-07:00","id":848219,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Transcend Incarnation</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Primum 9, completed Cypher [, Cannibalization?]<br /> <b>Effect</b>: You have amassed enough power and understand yourself to such a degree that you can transcend the limits of your Incarnation and adapt the abilities of another. You count as all of your Incarnations at all times (such as determining the effects of Going Loud).<br /> <b>Note</b>: This Merit can be taken multiple times, adding a new Incarnation each time.<br /> <br /> [<u>Comments</u>: This is mostly so other Incarnations can join in on the Exploit combining fun Analysts have when Going Loud (and for Analysts to pick up the other Incarnations' benefits). Currently, the benefits are very limited, though other Incarnation-dependent abilities (and a few of my own house rules) increase its value.]<br /> <br /> <b><u>Extraordinary Extradition</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Primum 7, Summon<br /> <b>Effect</b>: No matter where a pactee might run or hide, once the Demon owns their soul, they are completely its. You can use your connection to a target whose &quot;soul&quot; you own to pull them or yourself between spaces to the other's location, cashing in your claim and taking them as a Cover. Make a Primum roll - the target's Resolve as an Instant action, with success instantly transporting the Demon to the target's location, or the target to the Demon's location. If the roll fails, the Demon cannot attempt it again for 1 week, and the target knows what almost happened.<br /> <b>Note</b>: You must still physically possess the Soul Pact document to use this ability.<br /> <br /> [<u>Comments</u>: The failure condition (which <i>can</i> fail if the Demon has negative modifiers on them at the time) also offers some plot hooks in the vein of a desperate individual needing the troupe's help <i>ASAP</i>. Though maybe I should change to the roll to Contested and/or Resolve + Composure?]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-16-2016, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T13:31:54-07:00","id":848953,"title":"","content":"Some generic Supernatural Merits, and another for general Stigmatics. <hr /><br /> <b><u>Cryptid Form</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Stigmatic<br /> <b>Effect</b>: You have been touched by the God-Machine and its Occult energies deeper than most. While most of the time your are as human as anyone else (more or less), sometimes you transform into a monstrous creature (a Cryptid). Whenever you acquire wound penalties or your involuntary trigger (see Drawback, below) is invoked, you must make a Reflexive Extended action each turn, rolling Resolve + Composure toward a target number of successes equal to your Cryptid form's Resolve + Rank. Failing any roll results in immediate change, though the player can also choose to forgo the roll to change immediately. At the end of each Scene, you make the same roll against the same target number to change back. The three dot version of this merit means you have little to no control over your Cryptid other self's action, essentially making them a Storyteller character for the duration of the Transformation. The five dot version let's your character retain control, though role-playing your new form's influence is encouraged.<br /> <b>Drawback</b>: You acquire a Glitch which both marks you as odd, and can involuntarily trigger your transformation. Work with the Storyteller to determine an appropriate one that may come up occasionally in the Chronicle. Depending on player control and Cryptid strength, you may choose severity from mild to catastrophic. For Tells, failing to do the required action (or doing the forbidden action) triggers the transformation. For Brands and Emanations, determine what a suitable trigger might be based upon it (an Emanation of cold might trigger if the temperature is forcibly brought up, for instance).<br /> <b>Note</b>: Work with the Storyteller to develop your Cryptid Form. Abilities and Skills are <i>usually</i> derived from the character's, prior to the Cryptid template's modifications. Rank should usually be low, unless you are keeping it to the involuntary change version, or the game is fine with such a higher powered option.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: Behold! A Demon-friendly way to model &quot;werewolves&quot; and all sorts of other creatures. You could even model the Hulk with this as a Rank 4-5 Cryptid form of Bruce Banner, with something anger related as the triggering Glitch.]<br /> <br /> <b><u>Longevity</u> \u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 (Supernatural)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Mortal only (or qualifying micro and minor templates, like Stigmatic, obviously)<br /> <b>Effect</b>: You age at a much slower rate than most. You only age 1 year for every 2 that pass at one dot, and each additional dot halves the rate again, with the second dot meaning 4 years must pass for you to age 1, all the way up to 32 years to age 1 at five dots.<br /> <b>Note</b>: While not a drawback, per se, eventually your neighbors will wonder why you barely seem to get old. You will also eventually have to face everyone else you know growing older (than you) and dying, which might risk Integrity for some.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: The point of this was for longer lived individuals. The reason it appears here, on a Demon thread, is because this would fill in the &quot;want to live longer/forever&quot; niche in Pacts.]<br /> <br /> <b><u>Eternal Youth</u> \u2022\u2022 (Supernatural)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Mortal only<br /> <b>Effect</b>: Your body never progresses beyond the bloom of your youth, freezing your apparent age in your prime (usually the early 20s) for as long as you live. If you acquire this ability while already older, you regress to such an age at the rate of 1 year per day.<br /> <b>Note</b>: While you never suffer the ravages of aging (and thus, many of the accompanying health complications), anything that has determined your &quot;fated&quot; life span still takes effect (and you can still die normally from damage or a heart attack, of course). If you are fated to grow no only than 105, you will die mysteriously at that age even while looking young and (likely) vital. If you <i>lose</i> this Merit for any reason, you begin to age up to your true age at the rate of 1 year per day.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: Just because you bargained for long life doesn't mean youth comes with it. Such options cost extra.]<br /> <br /> <b><u>Ageless</u> \u2022 (Supernatural)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Longevity \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Effect</b>: You cease to grow older entirely, enduring centuries and even millennia just as you look now. While you can die just like anyone else, be it from infectious disease or having your head cut off, you never suffer any more of the ravages of age (than you already may have). Additionally, you cease scaring and will never develop cancer, henceforth.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: The final &quot;live forever&quot; package deal. Pacting for this will cost a hefty +6, or +8 if you need to get de-aged via Eternal Youth above. Better start assembling your &quot;assets&quot;. The scaring and cancer immunity were thrown in due to &quot;perfect cell replication&quot;.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-17-2016, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T14:01:07-07:00","id":848970,"title":"","content":"I love the idea of Cryptid Form.<br /> <br /> For Longevity, I'd have it halve the rate of aging per dot (1/2 at one dot, 1/32 years at 5) because that is how Lucifuge Status and the Longevity Aspect handled it in 1E","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T14:15:02-07:00","id":848980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=848970#post848970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the idea of Cryptid Form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I can see this spawning another Merit chain (like a micro template). Currently it is pretty free form, though. Not sure what room for growth there might be. (Maybe the ability to use some Adaptations in your &quot;human form&quot;?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=848970#post848970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Longevity, I'd have it halve the rate of aging per dot (1/2 at one dot, 1/32 years at 5) because that is how Lucifuge Status and the Longevity Aspect handled it in 1E</div> </div> </div> </div>It is done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-17-2016, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T20:28:41-07:00","id":849586,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Overclock (2 or 3 dots, not sure)</b></u><br /> <br /> System: By spending a point of (Willpower/Aether) you can send your Cover into overdrive while flying under the radar. Food, water, sleep... everything that makes your Cover human can go ignored for two days per point spent. By spending an additional point you can increase your processing power: books are finished in a matter of minutes instead of hours, days, or weeks. At the end of this time the demon must spend an hour recovering for every day it was overclocking and a day for every week it was overclocking. Going a month or more on overclock can risk permanent glitches in the Cover.<br /> <br /> Some things I'm unsure on with this - the number of dots necessary and the expenditure amount/pool. But I liked the idea of, if a demon really needs info in a hurry, being able to go into this state where they don't have to run the risk of keeping up their Cover - but it still costs them to keep going in some way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11491-thehallow1","name":"thehallow1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11491_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T07:00:19-07:00","id":849696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thehallow1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=849586#post849586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Overclock (2 or 3 dots, not sure)</b></u><br /> <br /> System: By spending a point of (Willpower/Aether) you can send your Cover into overdrive while flying under the radar. Food, water, sleep... everything that makes your Cover human can go ignored for two days per point spent. By spending an additional point you can increase your processing power: books are finished in a matter of minutes instead of hours, days, or weeks. At the end of this time the demon must spend an hour recovering for every day it was overclocking and a day for every week it was overclocking. Going a month or more on overclock can risk permanent glitches in the Cover.<br /> <br /> Some things I'm unsure on with this - the number of dots necessary and the expenditure amount/pool. But I liked the idea of, if a demon really needs info in a hurry, being able to go into this state where they don't have to run the risk of keeping up their Cover - but it still costs them to keep going in some way.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Considering how abnormal the behavior is, I think it'd risk Compromises. As far as finishing tasks in less time, There's an App, I mean Exploit for that (Swift Resolution).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T07:48:54-07:00","id":849711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=847531#post847531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deionscribe, if you think Lucifer Mode is too much for one Merit, know that I thought of a more modular version: a Supernatural Style, with each Maneuver having a Primum prerequisite. Some Maneuvers would be accessible in full Demonic Form without Going Loud.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Any chance we could see that Style, or others like it? I've tried thinking some (others) up, but most ideas I have are very dependent upon Demonic Form choices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T21:25:25-07:00","id":851580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=848953#post848953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some generic Supernatural Merits, and another for general Stigmatics. <hr /><br /> <b><u>Cryptid Form</u> \u2022\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Stigmatic<br /> <b>Effect</b>: You have been touched by the God-Machine and its Occult energies deeper than most. While most of the time your are as human as anyone else (more or less), sometimes you transform into a monstrous creature (a Cryptid). Whenever you acquire wound penalties or your involuntary trigger (see Drawback, below) is invoked, you must make a Reflexive Extended action each turn, rolling Resolve + Composure toward a target number of successes equal to your Cryptid form's Resolve + Rank. Failing any roll results in immediate change, though the player can also choose to forgo the roll to change immediately. At the end of each Scene, you make the same roll against the same target number to change back. The three dot version of this merit means you have little to no control over your Cryptid other self's action, essentially making them a Storyteller character for the duration of the Transformation. The five dot version let's your character retain control, though role-playing your new form's influence is encouraged.<br /> <b>Drawback</b>: You acquire a Glitch which both marks you as odd, and can involuntarily trigger your transformation. Work with the Storyteller to determine an appropriate one that may come up occasionally in the Chronicle. Depending on player control and Cryptid strength, you may choose severity from mild to catastrophic. For Tells, failing to do the required action (or doing the forbidden action) triggers the transformation. For Brands and Emanations, determine what a suitable trigger might be based upon it (an Emanation of cold might trigger if the temperature is forcibly brought up, for instance).<br /> <b>Note</b>: Work with the Storyteller to develop your Cryptid Form. Abilities and Skills are <i>usually</i> derived from the character's, prior to the Cryptid template's modifications. Rank should usually be low, unless you are keeping it to the involuntary change version, or the game is fine with such a higher powered option.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: Behold! A Demon-friendly way to model &quot;werewolves&quot; and all sorts of other creatures. You could even model the Hulk with this as a Rank 4-5 Cryptid form of Bruce Banner, with something anger related as the triggering Glitch.]<br /> <br /> <b><u>Longevity</u> \u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 (Supernatural)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Mortal only (or qualifying micro and minor templates, like Stigmatic, obviously)<br /> <b>Effect</b>: You age at a much slower rate than most. You only age 1 year for every 2 that pass at one dot, and each additional dot halves the rate again, with the second dot meaning 4 years must pass for you to age 1, all the way up to 32 years to age 1 at five dots.<br /> <b>Note</b>: While not a drawback, per se, eventually your neighbors will wonder why you barely seem to get old. You will also eventually have to face everyone else you know growing older (than you) and dying, which might risk Integrity for some.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: The point of this was for longer lived individuals. The reason it appears here, on a Demon thread, is because this would fill in the &quot;want to live longer/forever&quot; niche in Pacts.]<br /> <br /> <b><u>Eternal Youth</u> \u2022\u2022 (Supernatural)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Mortal only<br /> <b>Effect</b>: Your body never progresses beyond the bloom of your youth, freezing your apparent age in your prime (usually the early 20s) for as long as you live. If you acquire this ability while already older, you regress to such an age at the rate of 1 year per day.<br /> <b>Note</b>: While you never suffer the ravages of aging (and thus, many of the accompanying health complications), anything that has determined your &quot;fated&quot; life span still takes effect (and you can still die normally from damage or a heart attack, of course). If you are fated to grow no only than 105, you will die mysteriously at that age even while looking young and (likely) vital. If you <i>lose</i> this Merit for any reason, you begin to age up to your true age at the rate of 1 year per day.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: Just because you bargained for long life doesn't mean youth comes with it. Such options cost extra.]<br /> <br /> <b><u>Ageless</u> \u2022 (Supernatural)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Longevity \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Effect</b>: You cease to grow older entirely, enduring centuries and even millennia just as you look now. While you can die just like anyone else, be it from infectious disease or having your head cut off, you never suffer any more of the ravages of age (than you already may have). Additionally, you cease scaring and will never develop cancer, henceforth.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: The final &quot;live forever&quot; package deal. Pacting for this will cost a hefty +6, or +8 if you need to get de-aged via Eternal Youth above. Better start assembling your &quot;assets&quot;. The scaring and cancer immunity were thrown in due to &quot;perfect cell replication&quot;.]</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Added your Cryptid Form Merit to the GDoc. And placed those longevity-based Supernatural Merits in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/834294-merits-chronicles-of-darkness\">here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T07:44:19-07:00","id":855068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=851580#post851580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Added your Cryptid Form Merit to the GDoc. And placed those longevity-based Supernatural Merits in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/834294-merits-chronicles-of-darkness\">here</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I was waiting for a thread like that... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T13:15:20-07:00","id":855207,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Should I write up the general Supernatural Merits derived from Medium here, or there? Or are they (the following) even necessary with Ephemeral Adaptation?<br /> <br /> Spiritual Insight - Learn details (Ban, Bane, Influence, Numina, etc.) about Ephemerals who use your Open Condition (created via Medium).<br /> Spirit Trap - Apply the Open Condition to a warded circle/item/person, such that when an ephemeral Manifests there, they are trapped.<br /> Spirit Bargain - Allow for the ephemeral trapped above to be released upon fulfilling a number of requests.<br /> Spirit Calling - Allows for the services to be used at a later date, summoning the ephemeral from where-ever to provide them (each summoning counts as its own service?).<br /> Spirit Binding - Allows for ephemerals trapped to be bound into Fetishes.<br /> Counter-Possession - Allows for the Medium to Possess the ephemeral instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T14:09:48-07:00","id":855230,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of Spiritual Insight, but I want to say Hardened Exorcist did something similar? Or maybe that was a homebrew Style Merit based off of it I saw on the forums. Either way, more homebrew couldn't hurt. Spirit Trap seems like a really cool idea, but wouldn't they constantly apply the Resonant/Anchor/Infrastructure Condition to the warded area instead of the Open Condition? I think a few werewolf Rites would be a good starting point for that.<br /> <br /> Spirit Bargain sounds like something that could be roleplayed out, Spirit Calling sounds like an unusual Allies, Contacts, or Retainer Merit, but making it a Merit to <i>summon </i>Ephemeral Beings as a much quicker action than the Extended Research and Ritual action it normally does could be cool. Spirit Binding to make Fetishes sounds like a Wolf-Blooded Tell, so no less than three dots. Counter-Possesion sounds like a great idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T12:52:37-07:00","id":855906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=855230#post855230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of Spiritual Insight, but I want to say Hardened Exorcist did something similar? Or maybe that was a homebrew Style Merit based off of it I saw on the forums. Either way, more homebrew couldn't hurt. Spirit Trap seems like a really cool idea, but wouldn't they constantly apply the Resonant/Anchor/Infrastructure Condition to the warded area instead of the Open Condition? I think a few werewolf Rites would be a good starting point for that.<br /> <br /> Spirit Bargain sounds like something that could be roleplayed out, Spirit Calling sounds like an unusual Allies, Contacts, or Retainer Merit, but making it a Merit to <i>summon </i>Ephemeral Beings as a much quicker action than the Extended Research and Ritual action it normally does could be cool. Spirit Binding to make Fetishes sounds like a Wolf-Blooded Tell, so no less than three dots. Counter-Possesion sounds like a great idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Hardened Exorcist just makes using Abjurations, etc. easier, and let's you use your Vice. Not sure about the Homebrew expansion - I remember that thread, but not some of the details.<br /> <br /> Mediums can upgrade those Conditions to Open, which is necessary for a number of Manifestations. Spirit Trap makes it so any ephemeral that takes advantage of your generated Open Condition, gets trapped there. You could probably manage it normally, but the intent here is that this makes it sneaky.<br /> <br /> The idea behind Spirit Bargain was for mechanical support and enforcement. You can name successes (or something like that) in tasks, which the ephemeral has the option of accepting for automatic release. But then it <i>must</i> fulfill them, as if they were its Ban. &quot;Don't harm me afterward&quot; is recommended as one, but not strictly required.<br /> <br /> Spirit Calling is intended as a summoning effect - sorry if that wasn't clear. Now you can have your own Summons or Spirit-Pokemon!<br /> <br /> Yeah, Spirit Binding would make a decent independent Tell (if such doesn't already exist). I used Fetish as a short-hand, since the rules for that exist and are flexible. A Fetter (from Geist: the Sin-Eaters) is another option. No idea what a bound Goetic would be like, nor a bound Angel.<br /> <br /> Counter-Possession is another &quot;turn the tables&quot; trick, like Usurp Control (and, frankly, is equivalent/redundant if you use Ephemeral Adaptation with it). Let's <i>you</i> play with the ephemeral's power and abilities. Though it is likely to piss off such beings (and I'd rule Angels are considered Exiles while it is in effect).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T13:20:12-07:00","id":855932,"title":"","content":"Here's another Sleeve Integrator one: <hr /><br /> <b><u>Terms of Service</u> \u2022\u2022</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Sleeve Integrator, Occult \u2022\u2022\u2022, Subterfuge \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Effect</b>: Your occult insight has figured out how to trigger automatic pacts and clauses with Demons that use you as a Cover. You can state some action or service and conditions that a Demon must carry out if you succeed at a Resolve + Integrity roll vs the Demon's Wits + Primum. Any Demon that uses your Identity as a Cover gains a Transient Tell Glitch, compelling them towards the listed behavior (such as &quot;bring no willful harm to me&quot; or &quot;leave when asked&quot;). The Story Teller may determine that certain actions or prohibitions grant a bonus or penalty (to either party) depending on how advantageous or compromising they are, or merely rule them out entirely.<br /> <b>Drawback</b>: You must keep the terms and conditions (text/symbols written in or partially comprised of your own blood) on yourself prior to Sleeve Integration. If discovered and separated from you prior to the merger, this merit has no effect upon the Demon's behavior. Some Stigmatics tattoo critical terms to themselves, but this can also serve to give away your plan.<br /> <b>Note</b>: You can take this merit multiple times, adding a new set of terms and conditions for each instance.<br /> <i>Ephemeral Adaptation</i>: Treat the ephemeral entity as if it had such action as a Ban instead of a Tell Glitch. They roll Resistance + Rank to oppose you instead. Such compulsions last a Scene for Rank 1, a Day for Rank 2 or 3, a Week for Rank 4, and a Month for Rank 5.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: Now, even if you make use of the &quot;screw over the Demon&quot; Sleeve Integrator line of merits, you might stop the Demon from tearing you (or your life) apart in retaliation. Ephemeral duration was calculated by multiplying Rank * 2 to get the equivalent Primum. Not sure if copies should roll separately, or have all dependent upon a single roll.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-07-2016, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T04:07:09-07:00","id":860929,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8180\" data-vbnamecard=\"8180\">Deionscribe</a> Updated Cannibalization to note its interaction with Angelic Form Abilities. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=805235#post805235\">Link</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T04:35:34-07:00","id":860941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=860929#post860929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> Updated Cannibalization to note its interaction with Angelic Form Abilities. <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=805235#post805235&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Checking it out. Will update it on the GDoc when I'm back from the field.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T21:17:19-07:00","id":863473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=794945#post794945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry I missed this completely. I definitely like this a lot and can see its utility. I like the effect of it as is. It's powerful, indiscriminate, and is more manageable than the Self Destruct mechanic introduced in Interface. I guess I only have two questions: First, does this feel more like a merit, or, more like something all demons can do? Secondly, the drawbacks make sense, but I was wondering how you would feel about possibly tacking something on that played into the theme of letting loose with all that energy? Something like what you see in the latest (albeit mixed) run with Superman. They could have a condition that leaves their primiuim one less than where it was before they went loud and can only beat it by buying the next level of primium. The only reason I suggest this is that I can imagine this being used to clear out some serious angelic/supernatural threats with one shot. I hope that all makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Planning on revisiting that Outburst Merit of mine soon. And yeah, I think it does make more sense for it to work as an alternative to the self-destruct mechanics found in Interface. As for a drawback, perhaps the self-destruct should <i>also</i> damage the Demon, like maybe [10 - Cover] lethal damage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T06:28:30-07:00","id":863593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=863473#post863473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Planning on revisiting that Outburst Merit of mine soon. And yeah, I think it does make more sense for it to work as an alternative to the self-destruct mechanics found in Interface. As for a drawback, perhaps the self-destruct should <i>also</i> damage the Demon, like maybe [10 - Cover] lethal damage?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah I think some damage to the demon would be a good idea, but I feel like a roll of [10 - Cover] would make it possible to walk away significantly unscathed depending on the amount of cover they had upon use. Maybe make it just a flat roll of 5L, or maybe it could damage their Stamina and in turn reduce their health box number until they get into a new cover?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T06:44:15-07:00","id":863600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=863593#post863593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah I think some damage to the demon would be a good idea, but I feel like a roll of [10 - Cover] would make it possible to walk away significantly unscathed depending on the amount of cover they had upon use. Maybe make it just a flat roll of 5L, or maybe it could damage their Stamina and in turn reduce their health box number until they get into a new cover?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure I like the idea of it damaging Stamina. And just to clarify, it's automatic damage inflicted, not successes from a dice pool.<br /> <br /> As for why I made it [10 - Cover], my reasoning was that such an explosive way of Going Loud would be particularly lethal without something to buffer it (like, say, the solid Infrastructure of a high Cover). This can serve as a good reason to maintain low-quality Covers for very extreme Saboteurs. Or as a good way to strike back at whoever forced the Demon to Burn a well-lived Cover.<br /> <br /> Still, I am open to the possibility of a Condition being tied to Outburst. As well as make the damage [11 - Cover], so that the Demon always takes damage from self-destructing. And perhaps the damage could be resistant, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 04-11-2016, 09:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T06:57:23-07:00","id":863606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=863600#post863600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not sure I like the idea of it damaging Stamina. And just to clarify, it's automatic damage inflicted, not successes from a dice pool.<br /> <br /> As for why I made it [10 - Cover], my reasoning was that such an explosive way of Going Loud would be particularly lethal without something to buffer it (like, say, the solid Infrastructure of a high Cover). This can serve as a good reason to maintain low-quality Covers for very extreme Saboteurs. Or as a good way to strike back at whoever forced the Demon to Burn a well-lived Cover.<br /> <br /> Still, I am open to the possibility of a Condition being tied to Outburst. As well as make the damage [11 - Cover], so that the Demon always takes damage from self-destructing. And perhaps the damage could be resistant, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry about that misunderstanding. I see what you are getting at. The point you make in your second paragraph is pretty interesting and definitely works with the thematic qualitues of the merit.<br /> <br /> My only rationale behind a condition being connected to the merit is because of how strong it could be. Maybe the demon could suffer penalties to rolls that require aether or something that plays off of how traumatic the explosion is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T07:02:11-07:00","id":863609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=863606#post863606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry about that misunderstanding. I see what you are getting at. The point you make in your second paragraph is pretty interesting and definitely works with the thematic qualitues of the merit.<br /> <br /> My only rationale behind a condition being connected to the merit is because of how strong it could be. Maybe the demon could suffer penalties to rolls that require aether or something that plays off of how traumatic the explosion is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or either negatively affect his ability to use Covers, or roll ten dice for a Glitch roll. If we go with the Condition route, though, would it be an existing one or something new?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T07:20:40-07:00","id":863622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=863609#post863609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or either negatively affect his ability to use Covers, or roll ten dice for a Glitch roll. If we go with the Condition route, though, would it be an existing one or something new?</div> </div> </div> </div>Those both sound like good options.I think it really depends on how you see it coming up in the game and what characters have to do to acquire it. Right now I don't think any condition fits with i because of how diffeeent of a merit it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T07:24:53-07:00","id":863624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=863622#post863622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those both sound like good options.I think it really depends on how you see it coming up in the game and what characters have to do to acquire it. Right now I don't think any condition fits with i because of how diffeeent of a merit it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, now that I think about it, the Glitch roll might make more sense. You not only damage yourself by Going Loud, but also suffer a malfunction of sorts to your own systems.<br /> <br /> That said. If I go with it being a Merit, what do you suppose ita dot rating would be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T07:49:35-07:00","id":863642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=863624#post863624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, now that I think about it, the Glitch roll might make more sense. You not only damage yourself by Going Loud, but also suffer a malfunction of sorts to your own systems.<br /> <br /> That said. If I go with it being a Merit, what do you suppose ita dot rating would be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I definitely like the Glitch idea. Do you think making it a Catastrophic Glitch would be too much? <br /> <br /> I would say make it a four dot merit. That way people won't readily take it at creation to have a get out of jail free card. Plus it doesn't make sense thematically as anything lower. What are you thinking of for perquisites?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T21:59:39-07:00","id":864121,"title":"","content":"If anyone is wondering, yes, I'm still trying to figure out how the Lucifer Mode Supernatural Style would work.<br /> <br /> By the way, has anyone posted a Merit or Exploit that lets Demons give dots in Supernatural Merits to mortals as part of a Pact? Sure, Demons can give Gadgets, but sometimes the client doesn't like the idea of his powers being stolen, or they might be afraid of the installation surgery going wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T22:11:01-07:00","id":864124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Origina